{"run": "20261019-230338-t-stamp-book-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-stamp-book", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.178, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 1.0, "calls": 19, "obj_secs": {"smelter-down": 60}, "think_min": 0.3, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 6, "extra_looks": 2, "waste": 0.105, "cost_per_met": 0.178, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:take", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.5, "hand building": 0.15, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "waiting on jobs": 0.0, "thinking": 0.33}, "by_tool": {"say": 8, "inspect": 3, "look": 2, "build": 2, "techs": 1, "find": 1, "act": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to power. The stamped row came up with no power, so I ran poles 15 tiles from the grid, then hand-fed a dead boiler.", "2) Missing: any inventory (I started with 8 plates), a coal source near the base (nearest is about 97 tiles away), and a map of the whole base. I only found out the furnaces weren't live after stamping.", "3) Confusing: the build result said \"done\" even though the stamp had no power. Nothing failed outright, but I answered the \"put it somewhere open\" message after the row was already built, so I repeated myself.", "4) Next time: check the power connection straight after stamping, and post a board task so you could see what I was on. Then automate coal to the boilers before anything else, since the base is one empty chest from a blackout."], "phase": "holdout-before", "cycle": null}
{"run": "20261019-230338-t-backed-up-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-backed-up", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.414, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 41, "obj_secs": {"smelting-again": 181}, "think_min": 1.1, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 0, "looks": 17, "extra_looks": 6, "waste": 0.195, "cost_per_met": 0.414, "top_failures": [["FAILED stuck at N,N", 1], ["FAILED inventory full", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED inventory full", "FAILED stuck at N,N"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "mark", "production", "say", "stop", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 1.0, "hand building": 0.94, "walking": 0.54, "failed calls": 0.36, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.15}, "by_tool": {"act": 14, "look": 7, "find": 5, "say": 4, "wait": 3, "inspect": 2, "map": 2, "techs": 1, "mark": 1, "production": 1, "stop": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to walking: the coal, copper and iron patches are 85-130 tiles from the base, and a `look` near the coal patch dumped hundreds of lines of ore tiles.\n2) I was missing a map of what already exists. I found the working electric coal drills and the half-built copper ore belt only by walking up to them. I also ran out of inventory slots carrying 3000+ plates and 2000 coal.\n3) What confused me: the smelter at [gps=49,6] runs off an infinity chest and an energy interface, so I couldn't tell whether the full output chests were a real fault. The alerts also pointed at old burner drills that weren't worth refueling.\n4) Status: boilers fueled by hand (stopgap), copper ore belt ends at [gps=0,79] with no smelter, labs still idle. I had 24 inserters and a few furnaces ready for a copper smelter there.\n5) Next time I'd do the cheap checks first (production, board, alerts), then build one belt-fed coal and copper chain to the science block, instead of hand-fueling."], "phase": "holdout-before", "cycle": null}
{"run": "20261019-230338-t-coal-boilers-sonnet-i1", "scenario": "t-coal-boilers", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.31, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 39, "obj_secs": {"coal-to-boiler": 181}, "think_min": 1.3, "idle_min": 0.7, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 1, "looks": 14, "extra_looks": 7, "waste": 0.231, "cost_per_met": 0.31, "top_failures": [["FAILED nothing to take from iron-chest (iron-plate) (it holds nothing); nearest with iron-", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED nothing to take from iron-chest (iron-plate) (it holds nothing); nearest with iron-"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 1.48, "idle (nothing running)": 0.67, "crafting/fetching": 0.65, "walking": 0.22, "failed calls": 0.17, "hand building": 0.04, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.26}, "by_tool": {"say": 9, "act": 9, "inspect": 6, "wait": 6, "look": 3, "find": 3, "map": 2, "techs": 1}, "debrief": ["Belted: coal now flows from [gps=-33,64] over a splitter and ~110 tiles north to the boiler inserter at [gps=-27,-40]; the hand-fed chest is gone. Coal is arriving and the inserter is working. Note the patch is only 8 tiles with two burner drills (~0.5 coal/s shared), so more drills would be the next upgrade. The other boiler at [gps=-31,-43] has no inserter. What next?", "Debrief: 1) Most time went on fetching materials: the supply chests were ~90 tiles from the coal, and plates sat in a different chest than the one I tried first.", "2) Missing: a way to see all chest contents at once (marks showed nothing), and the \"belt it\" order was ambiguous until I found the hand-filled chest myself.", "3) Confusing: the first take from the plate chest returned empty. Also the connect tool's belt count and end orientation needed a manual check.", "4) Next time: ask which boiler the order meant, grab 200 plates up front, and add electric drills on the coal patch. Two burner drills can't feed both boilers at full load."], "phase": "holdout-before", "cycle": null}
{"run": "20261019-230338-t-circuit-sonnet-i2", "scenario": "t-circuit", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.401, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 32, "obj_secs": {"circuit": 302}, "think_min": 1.6, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 11, "extra_looks": 2, "waste": 0.062, "cost_per_met": 0.401, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "designs", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "production", "say", "stamp", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 1.87, "waiting on jobs": 0.66, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "walking": 0.23, "hand building": 0.17, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.62}, "by_tool": {"act": 8, "inspect": 5, "say": 4, "map": 3, "look": 2, "wait": 2, "stamp": 2, "build": 2, "techs": 1, "designs": 1, "marks": 1, "production": 1}, "debrief": [], "phase": "holdout-before", "cycle": null}
{"run": "20261019-231122-t-power-line-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-power-line", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.098, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 17, "obj_secs": {"power-the-block": 121}, "think_min": 0.2, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 6, "extra_looks": 1, "waste": 0.059, "cost_per_met": 0.098, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:take", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "techs"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.4, "blueprint/line building": 0.39, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.25}, "by_tool": {"say": 6, "look": 2, "act": 2, "inspect": 2, "find": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "build": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) The pole job took little time. The only slow part was finding poles, which were in a chest I only spotted with a wide look.", "2) I started with almost nothing and had no list of shared stock chests or what's in them. A marks list or an inventory search tool would have saved a look.", "3) The build line tool worked first try and the inspect check confirmed it. It's hard to see the power network's status, so I confirmed by checking that the assemblers were working.", "4) The bigger problems I found were not fixed. Coal is about 156 tiles away, so the boilers and furnaces have no automated fuel, and the labs are idle. Next time I'd ask earlier which of those to take first, and look at the whole base before touching the small job."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
{"run": "20261019-231122-t-power-line-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-power-line", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.146, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 21, "obj_secs": {"power-the-block": 121}, "think_min": 0.4, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 10, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.143, "cost_per_met": 0.146, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:take", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "production", "say", "techs"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.43, "hand building": 0.37, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.38}, "by_tool": {"say": 7, "find": 4, "look": 3, "inspect": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "build": 1, "act": 1, "production": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: the power line took the least time. build kind=line crafted and placed 10 poles in one call, and the assemblers were running right after. Most time went to chasing the fuel alerts: finding the boilers' hand-fed coal chest and the far coal patch around [gps=46,93].", "Missing: a fuel/supply map, so I could see at a glance where coal is mined and where it's used. find only searched about 32 tiles for entities, so I had to guess where the grid pole was. Confusing: the infinity chests feeding the gear assemblers, and why the base makes 135 coal/min yet the boilers sit on a hand-filled chest.", "Next time: after the power fix I'd have started the coal belt to the boilers sooner. I stopped to ask because it was a 160-tile build, and I should have picked a plan and posted a board task. Open issues: the boiler chest runs dry again (about 54 coal), 32 furnaces/drills are out of fuel near [gps=74,69], nothing is researching, and copper is at 0."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
{"run": "20261019-231122-t-cross-bus-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-cross-bus", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.137, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 22, "obj_secs": {"copper-across-bus": 181}, "think_min": 0.4, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 9, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.227, "cost_per_met": 0.137, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:take", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.32, "idle (nothing running)": 0.31, "hand building": 0.21, "failed calls": 0.08, "waiting on jobs": 0.04, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.36}, "by_tool": {"say": 5, "inspect": 4, "look": 2, "build": 2, "find": 2, "act": 2, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to finding materials. I started with 8 plates, and the stock chests near [gps=-11,-27] were far from the job, so the build tool's fetch and the walk to the chests took the longest.", "2) I was missing a list of shared stock (nothing was marked) and the fact that the chest inserter already existed. I only learned that after checking the map. 3) Confusing: the chest sat at x=-10.5 but you wrote -11, and the bus is 4 belts wide. I used undergrounds so it was never touched. The repeated 'inserter is set up' message arrived after I'd already done it. 4) Next time: inspect both ends first, mark the stock chests, and keep the boiler on a coal belt instead of hand-feeding it."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
{"run": "20261019-231122-t-cross-bus-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-cross-bus", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.133, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 21, "obj_secs": {"copper-across-bus": 181}, "think_min": 0.5, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 8, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.19, "cost_per_met": 0.133, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "wait"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.32, "waiting on jobs": 0.25, "hand building": 0.21, "failed calls": 0.08, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.46}, "by_tool": {"say": 6, "inspect": 4, "act": 3, "look": 2, "build": 2, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "find": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to finding materials. I started with 8 plates and had to look for the shared chests near [gps=-10,-28] before I could build anything. 2) I was missing a list of stock chests (marks was empty) and a way to know my own inventory and position up front. 3) The build line tool refused at first because it needed undergrounds. After I fetched them it handled the bus crossing and placed 28 tiles in one call. 4) Repeated messages about the inserter confused me: I'd already finished, and I only confirmed it by inspecting the chest. 5) Next time I'd mark the stock chests as providers and check the chest and inserter ends before planning. I'd also fix the alerts (boiler fuel, idle labs) sooner. I fueled the boiler but never queued research."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
{"run": "20261019-231122-t-belt-ore-sonnet-i1", "scenario": "t-belt-ore", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.193, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 30, "obj_secs": {"ore-to-furnaces": 181}, "think_min": 0.9, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 3, "undone": 0, "looks": 14, "extra_looks": 6, "waste": 0.3, "cost_per_met": 0.193, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1], ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", 1], ["FAILED nothing to take from iron-chest (transport-belt) (it holds N electronic-circuit); n", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED nothing to take from iron-chest (transport-belt) (it holds N electronic-circuit); n", "error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", "exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait", "work"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.39, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "blueprint/line building": 0.27, "failed calls": 0.08, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "waiting on jobs": 0.0, "thinking": 0.89}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 8, "say": 5, "act": 4, "look": 3, "build": 2, "find": 2, "wait": 2, "work": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "techs": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to finding materials. I had 8 plates and had to find the stock chests near [gps=-10,-28] for belts and undergrounds. 2) Missing: a list of shared stock locations up front, and no marks existed. 3) Confusing: the belt line tool started one row north of the drill belt's real end, because the coordinates are tile corners vs centers. The ore didn't flow until I hand-placed 2 linking belts, and I had to inspect to find that. 4) Boiler coal in the wooden chest is still a stopgap, not automated. 5) Next time: inspect the line's start and end tiles before calling build line, and check that ore reaches the furnaces, not just that the belt was placed."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
{"run": "20261019-231122-t-belt-ore-sonnet-i2", "scenario": "t-belt-ore", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.255, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 34, "obj_secs": {"ore-to-furnaces": 302}, "think_min": 0.9, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 3, "undone": 3, "looks": 13, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.294, "cost_per_met": 0.255, "top_failures": [["FAILED nothing to take from wooden-chest (iron-plate) (it holds nothing); nearest with iro", 4], ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1], ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED nothing to take from wooden-chest (iron-plate) (it holds nothing); nearest with iro", "error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", "exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "find", "inspect", "lesson", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 0.5, "hand building": 0.43, "failed calls": 0.23, "blueprint/line building": 0.03, "crafting/fetching": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.95}, "by_tool": {"say": 8, "inspect": 8, "act": 7, "map": 3, "build": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "find": 1, "wait": 1, "lesson": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on getting belts/undergrounds with only 8 plates; I'd checked nothing for materials first.", "2) Missing: a way to see belt ownership/use (empty belt looked dead, wasn't) and a plate stock; the line tool's start tile was off by one row vs the map, leaving two gaps I patched by hand.", "3) My mistake: I mined the x=88 belt for materials. Fixed with an underground, saved a lesson. Unfinished: boiler at [gps=-31,-43] has no fuel (the other boiler's chest has 42 coal), furnace output inserters looked unpowered, labs idle. Next time: take plates from furnaces first, inspect belt ends right after a line build."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
{"run": "20261019-231436-t-gear-cell-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-gear-cell", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.168, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 28, "obj_secs": {"gear-cell": 181}, "think_min": 0.5, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 2, "looks": 13, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.25, "cost_per_met": 0.168, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:blueprint", "act:rotate", "act:wait", "build", "designs", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "recipes", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.36, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "waiting on jobs": 0.17, "hand building": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 0.52}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 8, "say": 6, "find": 3, "act": 2, "wait": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "recipes": 1, "marks": 1, "designs": 1, "build": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: most time went to working out how to get parts, since I started with 8 plates and no copper. The build tool then crafted and placed everything in about 21s, which I didn't expect.", "What failed: the blueprint op placed both inserters facing the wrong way, so the assembler sat starved until I rotated them. I should have checked pickup/drop right after building. Missing: a way to see my own materials or stock without guessing, and to place inserters by pickup/drop in blueprint entities.", "Next time I'd place inserters with pickup/drop instead of a direction and inspect right after the build. I also misread the early low gear count as a fault when it was just slow output, so I'd measure the rate before reporting."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
