{"run": "20261019-231435-t-gear-cell-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-gear-cell", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.173, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 30, "obj_secs": {"gear-cell": 301}, "think_min": 0.7, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 0, "looks": 10, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.2, "cost_per_met": 0.173, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot craft assembling-machineN: missing ingredients", 1], ["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft assembling-machineN: missing ingredients", "error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "act:wait", "designs", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 1.23, "waiting on jobs": 1.16, "crafting/fetching": 0.26, "idle (nothing running)": 0.25, "failed calls": 0.22, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.7}, "by_tool": {"say": 8, "act": 6, "inspect": 5, "find": 3, "wait": 3, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "designs": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on getting 3 circuits for one assembler: I walked about 55 tiles to the copper ore and coal, then hand-smelted in a furnace.", "2) I started with almost no inventory and no copper. A starter kit (assembler, inserters, chest, pole) or a copper chest would have cut this to about two minutes.", "3) Confusing: gear output was slower than expected, and I never found out why. The inserter showed waiting_for_source_items and one inserter briefly showed no_power. I didn't measure the rate, so that's unverified.", "4) Next time I'd check what the base has in stock before walking anywhere. I'd also ask whether the exact spot you gave matters, instead of moving the build to the nearest pole."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
{"run": "20261019-231750-t-inserter-mall-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-inserter-mall", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.22, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 28, "obj_secs": {"inserter-mall": 121}, "think_min": 0.7, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 12, "extra_looks": 8, "waste": 0.286, "cost_per_met": 0.22, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.25, "walking": 0.22, "crafting/fetching": 0.17, "waiting on jobs": 0.12, "hand building": 0.09, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.74}, "by_tool": {"say": 8, "inspect": 6, "act": 5, "find": 3, "look": 2, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "map": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: the most time went to getting small electric poles. I started with no copper and no wood, so I walked about 60 tiles to old furnaces for copper plates and cut a tree for wood.", "Missing: a pocket stock of poles, copper and wood, and a way to see where plates sit. My inspect radius 12 on the copper field returned a huge dump of ore tiles.", "Confusing: act sometimes returned \"still running\" and my move ended at a different spot than I expected. I never posted a board task or set a done_when, which I should have done.", "Next time: take plates and circuits from the supply chests first, craft the poles before walking over, and put the task on the board at the start. I'd use a filtered inspect or find to locate copper plates."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
{"run": "20261019-231437-t-red-block-sonnet-i1", "scenario": "t-red-block", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.373, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 43, "obj_secs": {"red-block": 301}, "think_min": 1.4, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 13, "extra_looks": 2, "waste": 0.07, "cost_per_met": 0.373, "top_failures": [["FAILED no automation-science-pack in inventory", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED no automation-science-pack in inventory"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "act:wait", "board", "designs", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "production", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 2.68, "hand building": 0.71, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "walking": 0.23, "failed calls": 0.06, "crafting/fetching": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.42}, "by_tool": {"act": 12, "say": 10, "look": 5, "inspect": 5, "wait": 3, "techs": 2, "marks": 1, "designs": 1, "board": 1, "map": 1, "find": 1, "production": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/4: Most time went on the 120-tile round trip to carry packs from the science block at [gps=-27,87] to the labs at [gps=-23,-37]. Research is only moving because I hand-fed it.", "Debrief 2/4: I was missing a map of what feeds what. I didn't know the labs were 120 tiles from the pack assemblers or that the lab block runs on hand-filled chests. I also had no way to move packs automatically.", "Debrief 3/4: What confused me was the status text. The base line said nothing was researching, but the cause was distance, not a broken machine. The gear/science block was working fine. The lab-side assemblers were starved because their chests were empty.", "Debrief 4/4: Next time I'd run `find lab` and trace the whole pack-to-lab path first, then build a belt or inserter chain from the start. I'd also put a board task with a done_when check on lab uptime. Right now one lab is still starved and the setup stalls again once the chests run dry."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
{"run": "20261019-231640-t-red-block-sonnet-i2", "scenario": "t-red-block", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.283, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 26, "obj_secs": {"red-block": 241}, "think_min": 1.1, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 6, "extra_looks": 0, "waste": 0.0, "cost_per_met": 0.283, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "act:wait", "designs", "inspect", "look", "production", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 1.37, "walking": 0.23, "hand building": 0.21, "crafting/fetching": 0.07, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.11}, "by_tool": {"say": 8, "act": 8, "look": 3, "inspect": 2, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "designs": 1, "production": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: most time went to hand-crafting 6 assemblers, 14 inserters and 12 poles from raw plates, plus walking 85 tiles to the site.", "Missing: a stock of ready-made assemblers, inserters and poles, and a way to put science packs on a belt next to the iron/copper belts instead of in four separate chests.", "Nothing really failed. The only confusing bits were that the plate belts are fed from infinity chests, and that the boiler and fuel alerts didn't say whether my block would lose power.", "Next time I'd check the infinity chests first, craft the whole kit in one batch, and design a single output belt running to labs. Without that, the packs still have to be moved by hand to start research."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
{"run": "20261019-231915-t-inserter-mall-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-inserter-mall", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.23, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 30, "obj_secs": {"inserter-mall": 121}, "think_min": 1.3, "idle_min": 0.5, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 2, "looks": 13, "extra_looks": 5, "waste": 0.3, "cost_per_met": 0.23, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1], ["error: no entity called copper-cable (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", "error: no entity called copper-cable (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:configure", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.55, "hand building": 0.35, "waiting on jobs": 0.29, "failed calls": 0.27, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.32}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 10, "say": 6, "act": 6, "wait": 3, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "find": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/4: Most time went to a deadlock. Plain inserters on a mixed plate/gear belt filled the assembler with plates and then sat holding one, so gears never arrived. It took me three checks to see it.", "2/4: I was missing small-electric-pole materials (wood, copper). Hand-crafting was impossible, so I walked about 60 tiles to pick up a pole from spawn. A pole in the infinity chests or a copper source nearby would have saved that trip.", "3/4: Confusing: inspect showed the input inserter as \"working\" while it was actually stuck holding an item, and the ops reply \"thanks, that one's done\" came while it was still stalled. The map also doesn't show power coverage, so I had to work out the pole ranges by hand.", "4/4: Next time I'd use filter inserters from the start on any mixed belt, check pole coverage before placing, and build the full set of inserter, assembler and poles in one planned pass. I'd also verify output after about 60s before reporting."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
{"run": "20261019-232032-t-starved-sonnet-i1", "scenario": "t-starved", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.25, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 37, "obj_secs": {"red-running": 120}, "think_min": 1.0, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 1, "looks": 16, "extra_looks": 6, "waste": 0.189, "cost_per_met": 0.25, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"crafting/fetching": 0.73, "waiting on jobs": 0.49, "hand building": 0.17, "walking": 0.1, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.05}, "by_tool": {"say": 9, "act": 8, "inspect": 8, "look": 4, "find": 3, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "diagnose": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to working out why packs weren't reaching the labs. The belt fix was quick, but the missing output inserters and the labs sitting 80 tiles away took several inspects to find.", "2) I was missing a tool that traces an item's whole route from assembler to lab, and a way to see who owns the infinity chests. look's radius was also centered on me, not on the coordinates I passed.", "3) Confusing: a single reversed belt looked like a supply failure, and the \"NOTHING RESEARCHING\" alert hid the real causes: the wrong tech needing green packs, plus no output inserters. A move job also left me at an odd position (71,-26) once.", "4) Next time I'd check the whole chain end to end first (inputs, outputs, labs, tech pack needs) instead of fixing one link at a time. I'd also leave the build as a saved design. The infinity-chest inputs are a stopgap, so the real fix is mined, smelted supply by belt."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
{"run": "20261019-231335-t-smelter-column-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-smelter-column", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.445, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 10.1, "calls": 52, "obj_secs": {"eight-furnaces": 603}, "think_min": 1.6, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 4, "undone": 0, "looks": 18, "extra_looks": 8, "waste": 0.231, "cost_per_met": 0.445, "top_failures": [["FAILED no inserter in inventory", 7], ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", 1], ["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1], ["FAILED cannot craft inserter: missing ingredients", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft inserter: missing ingredients", "FAILED no inserter in inventory", "error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", "error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "designs", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "notes", "say", "techs", "wait", "work"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 5.43, "hand building": 0.52, "idle (nothing running)": 0.28, "failed calls": 0.18, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "crafting/fetching": 0.0, "thinking": 1.62}, "by_tool": {"act": 13, "say": 9, "inspect": 8, "wait": 7, "find": 6, "look": 3, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "designs": 1, "marks": 1, "work": 1, "notes": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/4: Most time went to materials, not the build. I started with 8 iron plates and no stone or copper, so I walked about 80 tiles each way for plates, stone and copper ore.", "2/4: Missing: a stocked depot chest, or any copper plates on hand. I couldn't craft all 16 inserters from the copper I had. Shortfall at the end: the 8th furnace came a trip later.", "3/4: Confusing: act has no inspect op, so a batch failed on that. Also, find name=iron-plate errors because it only searches entities, and I wasn't told that. The base was out of power at the time too, so I never confirmed the electric inserters at the new row ran.", "4/4: Next time I'd check the actual item counts and plan the whole shopping list (inserters, copper, stone, poles) before leaving, and make one trip. I'd also have posted a board task with done_when up front. The boiler on a hand-filled chest is still the biggest risk."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
{"run": "20261019-232003-t-steel-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-steel", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.242, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 35, "obj_secs": {"steel": 241}, "think_min": 1.0, "idle_min": 0.8, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 0, "looks": 14, "extra_looks": 6, "waste": 0.229, "cost_per_met": 0.242, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot place burner-mining-drill at N,N: blocked by burner-mining-drill@N,N", 1], ["FAILED cannot hand-craft stone-furnace (category crafting)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot hand-craft stone-furnace (category crafting)", "FAILED cannot place burner-mining-drill at N,N: blocked by burner-mining-drill@N,N"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "production", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.75, "waiting on jobs": 0.55, "walking": 0.35, "failed calls": 0.18, "hand building": 0.04, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.0}, "by_tool": {"say": 8, "act": 7, "inspect": 6, "look": 4, "wait": 4, "find": 3, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "production": 1}, "debrief": ["Steel is now at 16/min measured. Idle for orders: I can fix boiler/furnace fuel outages or get science going. Which first?", "Debrief 1/3: Most time went to materials. I arrived with almost nothing and had to walk about 60 tiles each way to find copper plates for inserters, plus mining rocks for stone.", "Debrief 2/3: I was missing a shared stock chest with inserters, furnaces and poles, plus a map of existing buildings. The idle copper furnaces with 33 plates each were luck. A small pole needs wood, and I had none.", "Debrief 3/3: Little failed. My first drill placement was blocked by an existing drill. The 'act' tool name didn't resolve once. Next time I'd check the inventory first, batch the material run into one trip, and use stamp/build rather than hand-placing 16 pieces. Steel measured 16/min at the end."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
{"run": "20261019-232418-t-deliver-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-deliver", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.19, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 1.0, "calls": 28, "obj_secs": {"chest-filled": 60}, "think_min": 0.5, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 0, "looks": 9, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.179, "cost_per_met": 0.19, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", 1], ["FAILED no copper-plate in inventory", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED no copper-plate in inventory", "error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:research", "act:take", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "hand building": 0.3, "waiting on jobs": 0.11, "failed calls": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.47}, "by_tool": {"say": 9, "act": 6, "look": 4, "inspect": 3, "find": 2, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/4: Most time went to finding things. My inventory was almost empty and the first look showed no stock. The depot chests at [gps=-13,-28] only turned up on a wider inspect. Once I found it, the 20 inserters and 50 belts took one call.", "Debrief 2/4: Missing: a stock listing for the whole base, and the wiring of the science block (which chest feeds which assembler). I put gears and copper in a chest that fed the gear assembler, not the science assembler, so I hand-fed the science assembler instead.", "Debrief 3/4: Confusing or failed: I queued research-speed-1 and it needs green science, which nothing makes. Labs now show starved (missing automation in 2), so the science is not reaching them. I never confirmed science output and I didn't get to the roughly 32 unfueled furnaces and drills around [gps=74,60].", "Debrief 4/4: Next time: check techs against the science packs available before queueing, read the machine wiring before feeding by hand, and verify that packs reach the labs before reporting success. Real fixes still open: coal belts for the boilers and furnaces, and automating the science feed."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
{"run": "20261019-231948-t-steel-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-steel", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.268, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 7.1, "calls": 40, "obj_secs": {"steel": 422}, "think_min": 1.0, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 0, "looks": 14, "extra_looks": 6, "waste": 0.2, "cost_per_met": 0.268, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot place stone-furnace at N,N: blocked by stone-furnace@N,N", 1], ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", "FAILED cannot place stone-furnace at N,N: blocked by stone-furnace@N,N"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 2.87, "failed calls": 1.11, "hand building": 0.76, "idle (nothing running)": 0.25, "walking": 0.23, "crafting/fetching": 0.01, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.97}, "by_tool": {"act": 11, "say": 7, "inspect": 7, "wait": 7, "look": 4, "find": 3, "techs": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to gathering parts by hand: walking ~60 tiles each way for stone and copper ore, then waiting on a stone furnace to smelt copper for the inserter circuits. 2) I was missing a stock of basic parts (inserters, furnaces, poles) and any note that infinity chests could supply plates. 3) Small confusions: a stray furnace already sat at my smelting spot, my first pole craft failed for lack of wood, and the first pole run didn't reach the grid until I added one more. 4) Next time I'd check the base for parts before walking out, take wood and stone on the first trip, and stamp a proven design instead of hand-placing 14 pieces. 5) Steel ended at 16/min, so the layout itself worked."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
{"run": "20261019-232053-t-starved-sonnet-i2", "scenario": "t-starved", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.518, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 67, "obj_secs": {"red-running": 120}, "think_min": 2.7, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 2, "looks": 38, "extra_looks": 27, "waste": 0.433, "cost_per_met": 0.518, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:move", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "post_task", "production", "say", "stop", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 2.0, "walking": 0.37, "hand building": 0.28, "crafting/fetching": 0.09, "looking": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 2.73}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 16, "act": 12, "say": 11, "map": 8, "look": 6, "diagnose": 4, "find": 3, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "post_task": 1, "production": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: (1) Most time went to tracing: two bad belt tiles (copper at [gps=46,2], iron corner at [gps=71,-26]) were quick fixes, but finding them meant walking belts by hand.", "(2) Missing: a belt-trace tool that shows where a line dead-ends, and a base overview (what feeds what). I also started with almost no items, so I had to take plates from furnaces.", "(3) Confusing: the base is only half-built. Coal drills feed chests, copper ore belt at [gps=0,78] dead-ends with no copper smelter, and the lab science assembler isn't fed gears. research-speed-1 also needs logistic packs nobody makes.", "(4) Next time I'd survey the whole chain first, then post a short plan. Coal: belt from the south coal field onto the free lane of the iron ore belt, plus a copper smelter at the ore belt end. I didn't get to build either, so coal and copper are still unfixed."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
