{"run": "20261019-232628-d4-library-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "d4-library", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.11, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 17, "obj_secs": {"two-more-smelters": 121}, "think_min": 0.3, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 4, "extra_looks": 0, "waste": 0.0, "cost_per_met": 0.11, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:take", "build", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "say", "techs", "wait", "work", "zone"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.95, "hand building": 0.12, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "waiting on jobs": 0.0, "thinking": 0.26}, "by_tool": {"say": 4, "build": 3, "look": 2, "zone": 2, "techs": 1, "find_space": 1, "inspect": 1, "act": 1, "wait": 1, "work": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to the second stamp, which paused once and needed a re-call. 2) I was missing power-grid info: I inferred wiring from inserter status rather than a direct \"connected to network\" check. 3) Confusing: the build result said \"built 0\" on the re-run, so I had to look to confirm it had finished. 4) Next time I'd verify power and fuel with a single inspect, and I'd have fixed the boiler and furnace coal outages earlier, since iron output kept dropping (205 to 19/min)."], "phase": "train-1", "cycle": 1}
