{"run": "20261019-233055-t-power-line-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-power-line", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.1, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 19, "obj_secs": {"power-the-block": 121}, "think_min": 0.3, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 6, "extra_looks": 2, "waste": 0.105, "cost_per_met": 0.1, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:take", "board", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "post_task", "say", "update_task", "wait"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.43, "hand building": 0.32, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "waiting on jobs": 0.0, "thinking": 0.28}, "by_tool": {"say": 7, "inspect": 4, "look": 1, "board": 1, "post_task": 1, "build": 1, "update_task": 1, "find": 1, "act": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: the order itself was quick. One build line placed 7 poles from the grid pole at 74.5,-52.5 to the assemblers, and I checked an assembler was working.", "What I was missing: a done_when check that works without a zone. Task #1's check failed with \"needs a zone\" and stayed in verifying even though the job was done. I also had no view of the whole base's fuel and power layout, so the coal problem showed up only as alerts.", "Nothing failed or confused me beyond that. Next time I'd give the board check a zone up front, and I'd go for the coal-to-boilers fix before the stopgap. Right now the boilers run from a hand-filled chest and 32 furnaces and drills are out of fuel."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
{"run": "20261019-233055-t-power-line-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-power-line", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.111, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 17, "obj_secs": {"power-the-block": 121}, "think_min": 0.3, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 8, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.176, "cost_per_met": 0.111, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:take", "build", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.42, "hand building": 0.32, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "waiting on jobs": 0.0, "thinking": 0.28}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 5, "say": 4, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "build": 1, "diagnose": 1, "find": 1, "act": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) The power line was quick, since build kind=line placed all 7 poles in one call. 2) The most time went to the unrequested alerts: the boiler, the unfueled furnaces and the idle labs. I only fixed the boiler, and only by hand. 3) Missing: a clear view of which alerts were mine to handle, and an item list. I started with almost nothing, and the line tool fetched or crafted the poles on its own. 4) Confusing: inspect at the start pole showed only one pole, so I couldn't tell by looking whether it joined the grid. I only knew once the assemblers showed working. 5) Next time I'd put the power task and a done_when check on the board first, then ask which alert to take."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
{"run": "20261019-233055-t-belt-ore-sonnet-i2", "scenario": "t-belt-ore", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.28, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 42, "obj_secs": {"ore-to-furnaces": 241}, "think_min": 0.8, "idle_min": 0.7, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 0, "looks": 24, "extra_looks": 14, "waste": 0.381, "cost_per_met": 0.28, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1], ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", "exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.67, "waiting on jobs": 0.5, "hand building": 0.33, "failed calls": 0.22, "crafting/fetching": 0.21, "walking": 0.21, "blueprint/line building": 0.09, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.85}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 14, "find": 5, "act": 5, "say": 5, "wait": 4, "look": 3, "map": 2, "build": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on walking 100+ tiles and gathering iron, because I started with 8 plates. 2) Missing: a nearby plate stock, and a look that works at a remote x,y instead of centering on me. 3) Confusing: the belt line tool started a row off and ended one tile short of the furnace belt, so I fixed both by hand. 4) Not done: the boiler and the 32 burners still depend on hand-fed coal, and the labs sit idle. 5) Next time I'd check the line's first and last tiles right after building, and craft materials while walking."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
{"run": "20261019-233055-t-cross-bus-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-cross-bus", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.208, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 31, "obj_secs": {"copper-across-bus": 241}, "think_min": 0.8, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 1, "looks": 16, "extra_looks": 7, "waste": 0.29, "cost_per_met": 0.208, "top_failures": [["FAILED route needs N transport-belt but you have N (and not the ingredients to craft N)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED route needs N transport-belt but you have N (and not the ingredients to craft N)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:move", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 0.93, "crafting/fetching": 0.48, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "hand building": 0.07, "failed calls": 0.01, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.85}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 11, "say": 5, "act": 5, "wait": 3, "look": 2, "find": 2, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to getting iron plates: I had 8, and the 31-belt run needed about 70 (gears from a chest, plates from furnaces 80 tiles away). 2) Missing: a shared stock chest of belts and plates, and a note saying the ops inserter was already placed. 3) Confusing: connect started the belt one row above the source belt, so nothing flowed until I rotated the last old tile; I should have checked flow right after placing, not by inspecting an empty chest. 4) Unfinished: boiler at [gps=-31.5,-43] is out of coal (its chest feed is empty-handed), 32 burners lack fuel, labs idle. 5) Next time: check the end tile alignment before connect and gather materials in one trip."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
