entory. The inserter drop landed at y+0.7 rather than a tile centre, which looked odd but worked. 4) Next time: check the inventory and ingredient chain (circuits need copper) before walking, and ask for a starter kit up front. I'd also set up a small copper furnace line first."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
{"run": "20261019-233634-t-red-block-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-red-block", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.269, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 34, "obj_secs": {"red-block": 241}, "think_min": 1.1, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 5, "looks": 12, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.235, "cost_per_met": 0.269, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:blueprint", "act:craft", "act:move", "act:place", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "designs", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "production", "say", "stamp", "techs", "wait", "work"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 0.64, "blueprint/line building": 0.6, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "hand building": 0.26, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 1.12}, "by_tool": {"say": 7, "inspect": 5, "act": 5, "wait": 3, "look": 2, "stamp": 2, "diagnose": 2, "techs": 1, "designs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "find": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: my earlier context was cleared, so I can't give details of what took longest. I only have the notes, and they are nearly empty.", "Missing: a roadmap and a board task with a done_when check. Without them, a fresh session sees \"NOTHING RESEARCHING\" and no hint of what I was building.", "Next time: I'd keep my notes current after every milestone, with coordinates and what's next. I'd also put research and labs first, since the dashboard shows 0/2 labs working and the base is producing no iron or copper."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
{"run": "20261019-233847-t-inserter-mall-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-inserter-mall", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.112, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 12, "obj_secs": {"inserter-mall": 121}, "think_min": 0.5, "idle_min": 0.2, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 4, "extra_looks": 0, "waste": 0.0, "cost_per_met": 0.112, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"walking": 0.23, "idle (nothing running)": 0.2, "hand building": 0.05, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.52}, "by_tool": {"say": 3, "act": 2, "inspect": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to working out where the assembler, inserters and chest could sit so the two existing poles powered them. I had no spare poles and no copper to craft any. 2) I was missing small poles, and the starting position was far from the job. The infinity chests solved materials once I walked there. 2b) I should have checked the chests earlier instead of looking for loose plates. 3) Nothing failed. The build worked first try, and the only confusion was the tile-center versus corner coordinates. 4) Next time I'd carry a few poles and check pole coverage first. I'd also fix the unattended alerts (boiler fuel, 32 burners out of coal, idle labs) before anything else, since they cost far more than an inserter mall."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
{"run": "20261019-233830-t-inserter-mall-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-inserter-mall", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.229, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 36, "obj_secs": {"inserter-mall": 121}, "think_min": 1.1, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 3, "undone": 0, "looks": 14, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.194, "cost_per_met": 0.229, "top_failures": [["FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory", 2], ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1], ["FAILED cannot place stone-furnace at N,N: blocked by transport-belt@N,N, transport-belt@N", 1], ["FAILED transport-belt won't accept wood", 1], ["FAILED transport-belt won't accept copper-ore", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", "FAILED cannot place stone-furnace at N,N: blocked by transport-belt@N,N, transport-belt@N", "FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory", "FAILED transport-belt won't accept copper-ore", "FAILED transport-belt won't accept wood"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "say", "stop", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 1.23, "walking": 0.23, "failed calls": 0.16, "idle (nothing running)": 0.02, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.07}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 9, "say": 7, "act": 7, "wait": 6, "look": 2, "find": 2, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "stop": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/4: The most time went on small electric poles. I started with 8 iron plates and no copper, so I walked about 57 tiles to the copper ore, hand-mined it and smelted one plate for the cable.", "Debrief 2/4: I was missing a few poles and copper plates in my starting kit. A shared stock chest or a way to request items would have saved the trip. I also had no way to set the infinity chests to hand out poles or cable.", "Debrief 3/4: Three things went wrong. First, the 'stop' op isn't valid inside act, and I lost one batch to that error. Second, the furnace placement failed because a belt was in the way. Third, the assembler jammed on the mixed iron/gear belt with a single input inserter, and the second inserter was unpowered until I added a pole. The inspect output ('working' while stuck, and an odd drop position) was misleading.", "Debrief 4/4: Next time I'd check the inventory and power pole reach first and ask for poles up front. I'd put two input inserters on a mixed belt from the start and run a pole along the whole row. I'd also check inserter status right after placing it instead of waiting."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
{"run": "20261019-233634-t-red-block-sonnet-i1", "scenario": "t-red-block", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.313, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 43, "obj_secs": {"red-block": 301}, "think_min": 1.3, "idle_min": 0.7, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 1, "looks": 16, "extra_looks": 8, "waste": 0.209, "cost_per_met": 0.313, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:rotate", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "designs", "diagnose", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "stamp", "techs", "wait", "work"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 0.67, "idle (nothing running)": 0.67, "blueprint/line building": 0.57, "hand building": 0.33, "walking": 0.22, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.26}, "by_tool": {"act": 8, "inspect": 8, "wait": 6, "say": 5, "look": 4, "stamp": 3, "diagnose": 2, "techs": 1, "designs": 1, "find_space": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to power: my `connect` poles left an 8.5-tile gap and an inserter out of pole range, so I found it only after the stamp showed no_power. 2) I was missing a way to see the starting inventory; I had to guess that the infinity chests were fair to take plates from (take caps at 100 per call). 3) The stamp's footprint hit an unseen belt at x=0, so I rotated it 90 and rotated one belt end to feed it. 4) Status checks showed stale no_power right after building, which caused extra inspects. 5) Next time I'd check stamp footprints and pole spacing (max 7.5) before building, and put the output chest in from the start. Red science ran at 28/min at the end."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
{"run": "20261019-233922-t-steel-sonnet-i2", "scenario": "t-steel", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.223, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 25, "obj_secs": {"steel": 302}, "think_min": 1.0, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 9, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.16, "cost_per_met": 0.223, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "production", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 1.31, "waiting on jobs": 0.84, "crafting/fetching": 0.24, "walking": 0.23, "failed calls": 0.05, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.0}, "by_tool": {"act": 8, "say": 5, "look": 3, "inspect": 2, "find": 2, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "wait": 1, "production": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on the supply run. I started with 8 plates and no stone or copper, so I walked about 60 tiles each way to the stone and copper patches and smelted a few copper plates by hand for the inserters. 2) What I was missing: a stock of furnaces, inserters and poles to pull from, plus a note saying the infinity chests at the belt were free to take iron and coal from. I only found that by inspecting them. 3) Nothing failed. The one surprise was that the furnaces filled with iron before coal, so I hand-primed 2 coal each, and the belt then supplied the rest. 4) Steel now measures 16/min, up from 4 and 12 in earlier readings. The layout is 4 separate chests, not one. 5) Next time I'd check marks and chests for materials first, then batch all crafting and placing into one queue."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
{"run": "20261019-234100-t-starved-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-starved", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.44, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 47, "obj_secs": {"red-running": 120}, "think_min": 2.2, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 2, "looks": 27, "extra_looks": 18, "waste": 0.447, "cost_per_met": 0.44, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot craft inserter: missing ingredients", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft inserter: missing ingredients"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:move", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "production", "say", "techs", "wait", "work"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 0.49, "hand building": 0.37, "idle (nothing running)": 0.26, "walking": 0.15, "looking": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "crafting/fetching": 0.0, "thinking": 2.22}, "by_tool": {"find": 9, "act": 8, "inspect": 6, "say": 6, "map": 6, "look": 5, "wait": 4, "techs": 1, "work": 1, "production": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/3: Fixed so far: a belt tile facing west at [gps=46,2] (red science) and the iron plate belt's last tile at [gps=71,-26] pointing north instead of turning west. I also queued research. The plate line was backed up and the main belt empty because of that one tile, and it took the most time to find: I traced the belt by hand across a 100-tile run.", "Debrief 2/3: I was missing a belt-continuity checker and a power/fuel overview. The root problem is that coal is hand-fed to the boilers at [gps=-27,-42] and to the furnaces, and the coal field at [gps=43,103] is 140+ tiles away. I was partway into building coal belts (belts crafted, nothing placed) when you called time. Red packs at [gps=51,5] also have no output path to the labs.", "Debrief 3/3: Next time I'd start with fuel and power (coal belt to the boilers and furnace ore lane), since the boilers will run dry within minutes and stop the coal drills too. Hand-crafting 170 belts is slow; I'd use the belt assembler. I stopped as asked."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
{"run": "20261019-234048-t-steel-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-steel", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.162, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 23, "obj_secs": {"steel": 241}, "think_min": 0.7, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 9, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.13, "cost_per_met": 0.162, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "recipes", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 0.61, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "walking": 0.23, "hand building": 0.17, "crafting/fetching": 0.16, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.66}, "by_tool": {"say": 5, "act": 4, "inspect": 4, "find": 3, "wait": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "recipes": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to getting materials: I started with 8 plates and no stone, so I walked 60 tiles to mine stone and pulled iron and coal from the infinity chests. 2) I was missing copper, so no circuits and no electric inserters. I used burner inserters instead, and the 4 output ones need hand-fuelling. 3) Confusing: the infinity chests weren't flagged as supply, and find only showed 2 empty iron chests as storage. A stock chest would have saved the stone trip. 4) Nothing failed. The first-try layout worked, and steel measured 4/min. 5) Next time I'd check for a stocked provider chest first and batch the mining and crafting into one queue. I'd also swap in electric inserters as soon as copper exists."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
{"run": "20261019-234132-t-starved-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-starved", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.409, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 48, "obj_secs": {"red-running": 120}, "think_min": 2.0, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 2, "looks": 29, "extra_looks": 20, "waste": 0.479, "cost_per_met": 0.409, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "build", "diagnose", "find", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "map", "post_task", "production", "say", "techs", "wait", "zone"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.73, "hand building": 0.39, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "failed calls": 0.15, "looking": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 2.04}, "by_tool": {"say": 8, "map": 8, "find": 7, "inspect": 7, "act": 4, "look": 3, "build": 3, "diagnose": 2, "techs": 1, "production": 1, "wait": 1, "post_task": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief. Most time went on tracing why red science was dead: the base had no copper at all and the ore line dead-ended at [gps=0,79].", "Missing: a one-call \"follow this belt to its end\" and a power/fuel overview. I walked the maps by hand and misread the ore legend once (c is copper, k is coal).", "Done: fixed the wrong-way belt at [gps=46,2], extended the ore belt from [gps=0,79] up to [gps=0,0] and east to [gps=34,0], and rerouted the coal belt at [gps=23,101] onto the ore belt's other lane. Not done: the furnaces, so no copper is smelted yet, and the labs still have no packs.", "Still broken: the boiler at [gps=-31,-43] is out of fuel, and the power chest is fed by hand. I'd fix the power coal feed first, then finish the smelter row (about 10 furnaces at [gps=14,3]), then belt plates to the science assemblers."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
{"run": "20261019-234148-t-brownout-sonnet-i1", "scenario": "t-brownout", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.228, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 35, "obj_secs": {"power-steady": 241}, "think_min": 0.9, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 0, "looks": 18, "extra_looks": 8, "waste": 0.286, "cost_per_met": 0.228, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1], ["FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory", 1], ["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", "FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory", "error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "hand building": 0.3, "walking": 0.29, "waiting on jobs": 0.03, "looking": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.93}, "by_tool": {"say": 8, "inspect": 7, "act": 6, "find": 5, "look": 4, "wait": 2, "diagnose": 2, "techs": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on walking. The site at [gps=-14,49] is about 50 tiles from the materials chests, and I made two round trips because I forgot the pole.", "2) I was missing a spare pole, copper for crafting one, and a quick way to see whether a site is on its own power grid. I had to guess that from the pole positions.", "3) What confused me: the first \"@serf Your call\" message about the boiler and the pond was ambiguous, so I went to the wrong boiler first. I also took a pole from a line I didn't check, and it may have cut power to something.", "4) Next time I'd check the whole supply chain before I touch anything: power per site, coal to the boilers, then science. The labs are still idle and I never got to them."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
{"run": "20261019-234503-t-deliver-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-deliver", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.122, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 1.0, "calls": 17, "obj_secs": {"chest-filled": 60}, "think_min": 0.2, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 7, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.176, "cost_per_met": 0.122, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:take", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.16, "waiting on jobs": 0.13, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.25}, "by_tool": {"say": 4, "find": 3, "act": 3, "look": 2, "inspect": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to walking: the stock chests at [gps=-10,-28] are about 30 tiles from the delivery chest, and the boilers are 66 tiles out. 2) I was missing a quick list of what each chest holds. I had to inspect a whole area to find the inserter and belt stock. 3) Nothing failed. The first look showed only 8 plates in my pocket, so I wasn't sure stock was meant for me, and I took it anyway. 4) Next time I'd check the boiler and fuel alerts before taking orders, and I'd automate coal to the boilers instead of hand-feeding. 5) Still open: the labs have no science, and the 32 fuel-starved drills near [gps=74,69] need a coal belt."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
{"run": "20261019-234602-d4-library-sonnet-i1", "scenario": "d4-library", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.097, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 15, "obj_secs": {"two-more-smelters": 121}, "think_min": 0.2, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 3, "extra_looks": 0, "waste": 0.0, "cost_per_met": 0.097, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "build", "find_space", "look", "say", "techs"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 1.19, "hand building": 0.16, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.2}, "by_tool": {"say": 8, "look": 2, "build": 2, "techs": 1, "find_space": 1, "act": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: the two stamps took the most time, about 40s each, and the build controller fetched and crafted everything itself even though I started with almost no items.", "I was missing a way to check that the stamp's poles tied into the grid. I inferred it from inserter status (waiting_for_source_items, not no_power).", "The second stamp returned \"paused\" with 0 ghosts left, which was confusing. Its east six furnaces also came out with no fuel, while the west six had 10 coal each.", "The same ops message arrived three times after the work was already done, so I answered it twice with no new information.", "Next time I'd put the order on the board with a done_when check, and fuel the furnaces as part of the build. I'd also fix the idle labs and the hand-fed boiler earlier, since those cost more than the smelters did."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
{"run": "20261019-234448-t-deliver-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-deliver", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.227, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 32, "obj_secs": {"chest-filled": 241}, "think_min": 0.7, "idle_min": 1.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 12, "extra_looks": 8, "waste": 0.281, "cost_per_met": 0.227, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 1.25, "waiting on jobs": 0.95, "hand building": 0.38, "crafting/fetching": 0.03, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 0.69}, "by_tool": {"say": 8, "act": 6, "find": 5, "inspect": 4, "wait": 4, "look": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "map": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: most time went to the crafting queue (50 belts plus 20 inserters by hand) and the 90-tile walks between the iron, copper and chest sites.", "Missing: an inventory or stock overview. I didn't know the furnaces held about 90 plates each until I inspected them, and the base had no shared plate chest.", "Confusing: your \"take them from stock or craft them\" message had no referent, and the same goes for my own first assumptions about what was available. I also took coal from furnaces that were already short of fuel, which was a mistake.", "Next time: check furnace outputs before crafting anything, put the order on the board with a done_when check, ask for clarification as soon as a message is ambiguous, and never take fuel from machines that need it."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
{"run": "20261019-233310-t-smelter-column-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-smelter-column", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": false, "score": 0.3125, "objectives": 1, "met": 0, "cost": 0.842, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 12.1, "calls": 106, "obj_secs": {}, "think_min": 5.6, "idle_min": 2.6, "failed_calls": 4, "undone": 3, "looks": 40, "extra_looks": 16, "waste": 0.217, "cost_per_met": null, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot place stone-furnace at N,N: blocked by small-electric-pole@N,N; nearest free", 1], ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): can't route transport-belt: no route found within s", 1], ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1], ["FAILED no path to N,N (blocked by water/cliffs/buildings?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", "FAILED cannot place stone-furnace at N,N: blocked by small-electric-pole@N,N; nearest free", "FAILED no path to N,N (blocked by water/cliffs/buildings?)", "exception: line failed after N leg(s): can't route transport-belt: no route found within s"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:configure", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "board", "build", "designs", "diagnose", "find", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "notes", "production", "say", "status", "techs", "wait", "zone"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 2.58, "hand building": 2.02, "crafting/fetching": 1.01, "waiting on jobs": 1.0, "walking": 0.74, "blueprint/line building": 0.52, "failed calls": 0.14, "looking": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 5.62}, "by_tool": {"act": 24, "inspect": 17, "say": 15, "wait": 14, "look": 9, "map": 7, "build": 4, "techs": 2, "designs": 2, "find": 2, "find_space": 2, "diagnose": 2}, "debrief": ["Debrief: most time went to bootstrapping copper plates (no copper, so no inserters or circuits) and to waiting on hand-crafts and the furnace.", "Missing: a copper plate stock and a quick way to see where the infinity chests feed (they supply the iron ore and coal). The alerts also pointed at an old burner outpost instead of the real shortage, which is no science packs.", "Confused/failed: the repeated chest message, which I couldn't match to any belt. Also, the copper column is stamped at [gps=14,65] but not finished. Coal is arriving, yet several furnaces are still unfueled and nothing has reached the plate output yet. Its output belt at [gps=24,64] isn't connected to anything.", "Next time: first ask what the target is (science packs), build copper before anything else, and verify the coal filter inserter at [gps=10,58] is delivering. Also hand-fuel the burner outpost last, since it's a stopgap.", "Refueled the power plant boilers at [gps=-31,-43]. That's hand-fed, so I'll automate it later. The labs are here at [gps=-25,-37], so red science goes here, and copper plates are now flowing at about 135/min."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
