{"run": "20261019-234437-t-brownout-sonnet-i2", "scenario": "t-brownout", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.93, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 8.1, "calls": 102, "obj_secs": {"power-steady": 482}, "think_min": 4.1, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 3, "looks": 48, "extra_looks": 22, "waste": 0.265, "cost_per_met": 0.93, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1], ["FAILED nothing to take from iron-chest (iron-gear-wheel) (it holds nothing); nearest with ", 1], ["FAILED nothing to take from iron-chest (iron-plate) (it holds nothing); nearest with iron-", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED nothing to take from iron-chest (iron-gear-wheel) (it holds nothing); nearest with ", "FAILED nothing to take from iron-chest (iron-plate) (it holds nothing); nearest with iron-", "exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:build_ghosts", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "designs", "diagnose", "find", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "post_task", "production", "recipes", "say", "stop", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 2.17, "hand building": 1.33, "walking": 0.68, "blueprint/line building": 0.64, "crafting/fetching": 0.51, "failed calls": 0.04, "looking": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 4.08}, "by_tool": {"act": 29, "inspect": 18, "map": 9, "diagnose": 7, "say": 7, "wait": 7, "look": 6, "find": 6, "build": 5, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "recipes": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: (1) Most time went to walking 100+ tiles between power, smelters, copper field and the base chests, and to tracing the broken iron and copper lines by hand. (2) I was missing a belt-trace tool that shows where a belt ends, and a list of which chests hold inserters, belts or circuits. (3) look and inspect centered on me instead of my x,y, so I wasted calls; inspect radius also dumped huge outputs. (4) Confusing: the infinity-chest test rigs and mid-air dead-end belts made it hard to tell intent from breakage. (5) Next time I'd stock a crafting kit (belts, inserters, poles, furnaces) before leaving base and trace belts end to end first. State now: power fixed, iron flowing, copper smelter (6 furnaces) built at [gps=3,73] but its plate belt to the base is not laid yet, so labs are still idle."], "phase": "train-2", "cycle": 2}
{"run": "20261019-235426-t-power-line-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-power-line", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.121, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 19, "obj_secs": {"power-the-block": 121}, "think_min": 0.3, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 7, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.158, "cost_per_met": 0.121, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:take", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.44, "blueprint/line building": 0.38, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "waiting on jobs": 0.0, "thinking": 0.3}, "by_tool": {"say": 6, "find": 3, "look": 2, "act": 2, "inspect": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "build": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to finding materials. I started with 8 plates, so I had to locate the pole chest at [gps=-12,-27] before the line build, which then took one call. 2) Missing: a single overview of shared chests and a nearby coal source. I found coal only 160 tiles away, which I only learned late. 3) Confusing: the repeated \"use small poles\" message arrived after I'd already done it, and I couldn't tell if it meant a different pole. 4) Unresolved: the boiler refuel was a hand stopgap. The 32 unfueled furnaces and drills and the idle labs are still untouched. 5) Next time I'd check power and fuel alerts first, then put the coal belt on the board as a task before anything else."], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
{"run": "20261019-235426-t-power-line-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-power-line", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.2, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 29, "obj_secs": {"power-the-block": 121}, "think_min": 0.6, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 11, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.103, "cost_per_met": 0.2, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:take", "build", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 0.58, "blueprint/line building": 0.42, "walking": 0.41, "hand building": 0.05, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.61}, "by_tool": {"say": 8, "look": 6, "act": 5, "inspect": 2, "find": 2, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "build": 1, "diagnose": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to walking: the coal field, the boilers at [gps=-31,-43] and the iron field at [gps=80,68] are 150+ tiles apart, so one refuel run took several minutes.", "2) The pole line was easy: build kind=line crafted and placed the 7 poles itself. Missing: a quick list of which machines are out of fuel with positions, and a way to see where coal is stocked. I found it by trial.", "3) Nothing failed, but the fuel alerts (32 machines) pointed at hand-fed burners with no belt, and one insert call per machine was slow. A bulk refuel-in-zone action would help. I never checked that the boilers were actually steaming again, and the labs are still idle with copper at 0.", "4) Next time: after the power fix I'd get coal automated first (belt or electric drills to the boilers and the iron field), then copper smelting, then science. Hand-fueling burner machines just comes back as another outage."], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
{"run": "20261019-235426-t-belt-ore-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-belt-ore", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.169, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 19, "obj_secs": {"ore-to-furnaces": 181}, "think_min": 0.4, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 8, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.263, "cost_per_met": 0.169, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:move", "act:take", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.61, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "waiting on jobs": 0.19, "failed calls": 0.08, "crafting/fetching": 0.01, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.37}, "by_tool": {"say": 5, "inspect": 4, "look": 2, "act": 2, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "find": 1, "map": 1, "build": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: most time went to the first build call failing for lack of undergrounds and belts, so I walked back to the supply chests at spawn, then crafted. I was missing the route facts (where the ore belt ended, which belt crosses it) and the location of the supply chests. I found the chests only by looking around. `find` was capped at radius 32 and returned only the belts nearest spawn, so I used `map` to see the real belt end. Nothing else failed, and `connect` handled the underground crossing well. Next time I'd check `marks` and the nearby chests for stock before the first build, and I'd raise the boiler-fuel and idle-labs alerts earlier, since I never got to them."], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
{"run": "20261019-235426-t-belt-ore-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-belt-ore", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.204, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 32, "obj_secs": {"ore-to-furnaces": 181}, "think_min": 0.7, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 3, "undone": 1, "looks": 14, "extra_looks": 5, "waste": 0.281, "cost_per_met": 0.204, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): this line would feed into someone's belt at N,N; pi", 1], ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1], ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", "exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", "exception: line failed after N leg(s): this line would feed into someone's belt at N,N; pi"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:move", "act:place", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 0.4, "walking": 0.21, "blueprint/line building": 0.21, "failed calls": 0.19, "hand building": 0.04, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.72}, "by_tool": {"say": 6, "inspect": 6, "act": 4, "look": 3, "find": 3, "build": 3, "wait": 3, "map": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to fixing my belt line: connect treated my coordinates as tile corners vs belt centers, so it started one tile off and ended one tile short of the furnace belt, and I needed two manual fixes.", "2) Missing: a way to see the chest of spare belts and undergrounds up front (I only found them by luck at [gps=-7,-29]), and a map that shows belt tile centers. 3) Confusing: my position jumped to the base while I was meant to be walking to the drills. 4) Next time: inspect the exact first and last belt tiles before calling connect, and verify the join with an ore-on-belt check right after. Left alone: boiler fuel, 32 unfueled burners, idle labs."], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
{"run": "20261019-235640-t-cross-bus-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-cross-bus", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.142, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 26, "obj_secs": {"copper-across-bus": 181}, "think_min": 0.5, "idle_min": 0.5, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 1, "looks": 12, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.192, "cost_per_met": 0.142, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:mine", "act:rotate", "act:take", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.5, "blueprint/line building": 0.32, "failed calls": 0.08, "hand building": 0.01, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "waiting on jobs": 0.0, "thinking": 0.51}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 8, "say": 5, "wait": 3, "look": 2, "build": 2, "act": 2, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "find": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) The most time went to finding materials. I started with 8 plates, and the stock chests were 100 tiles away at [gps=-11,-27]. 2) Missing: a list of shared stock locations up front, since I only found it by searching for chests. 3) The line tool ended the belt facing north into a wrong tile, so I rotated it and removed the extra belt by hand. Its result text also didn't say that the route had ended the wrong way. 4) You said \"not done yet\", but the copper was already flowing. I only checked once, so I should have shown the chest rising over several minutes in my first report. 5) Next time I'd check the stock chests and the belt end tile before building, and put the task on the board with a rate check."], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
