{"run": "20261019-235741-t-smelter-column-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-smelter-column", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.267, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 28, "obj_secs": {"eight-furnaces": 241}, "think_min": 1.2, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 16, "looks": 9, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.714, "cost_per_met": 0.267, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:blueprint", "act:clear_ghosts", "act:rotate", "build", "designs", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "post_task", "say", "stamp", "techs", "update_task", "wait", "work"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.71, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "hand building": 0.02, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "waiting on jobs": 0.0, "thinking": 1.25}, "by_tool": {"say": 5, "inspect": 4, "map": 3, "look": 2, "act": 2, "build": 2, "wait": 2, "update_task": 2, "techs": 1, "designs": 1, "marks": 1, "work": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief. Most time went on working out the layout: the my-smelter stamp was a 6-furnace design with its own input belt, so I cleared it and hand-placed 8 furnaces with shared poles.", "Missing: a note on what the stamped designs expect (which side input and output are on, ghost orientation), and inserter direction in blueprint entities. \"south\" meant pickup-from-south, so all 16 inserters came out backwards and I had to rotate them.", "Confused me: the board done_when \"exists\" check needs a zone, so task #1 can't pass, and clear_ghosts is only an act op, which I first called as a tool and it failed. Next time I'd use pickup/drop on inserters, check the stamp ghosts before building, and put a zone in done_when."], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
{"run": "20261019-235953-t-gear-cell-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-gear-cell", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.168, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 31, "obj_secs": {"gear-cell": 301}, "think_min": 0.7, "idle_min": 0.6, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 11, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.129, "cost_per_met": 0.168, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 1.4, "idle (nothing running)": 0.59, "hand building": 0.58, "walking": 0.24, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 0.66}, "by_tool": {"say": 9, "act": 6, "inspect": 6, "find": 3, "wait": 3, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: most time went into getting copper, because I started with 8 plates and no circuits. I walked about 60 tiles to the copper patch, hand-mined and smelted 15 ore, then crafted the parts.", "I was missing a stock of copper plates or circuits, and I only learned the iron source was an infinity chest by inspecting it. The finder also couldn't search for plates, only for ore.", "Nothing really failed. Two things confused me: I reported the gear count twice without checking it against the 40 target, and the belt only carried plates on one lane, so the assembler sometimes starved.", "Next time I'd check for stock chests first and grab copper and circuits in one trip. I'd also read the target number before reporting, and say up front that the assembler is limited by belt throughput."], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
{"run": "20261020-000158-t-red-block-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-red-block", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.334, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 6.0, "calls": 30, "obj_secs": {"red-block": 362}, "think_min": 2.0, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 9, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.1, "cost_per_met": 0.334, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "act:wait", "designs", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 1.52, "hand building": 0.51, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "walking": 0.23, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 2.04}, "by_tool": {"act": 8, "say": 6, "look": 4, "inspect": 4, "techs": 3, "wait": 2, "designs": 1, "marks": 1, "map": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on reading the state (look, techs, the boiler inspect); I only queued research and never built anything. 2) I was missing a clear order from you and a roadmap. The alerts gave me three problems with no priority. 3) Confusing: the labs show 0/2 working and \"missing automation\" even though research is queued, and I didn't find out why. The red packs are sitting in chests at [gps=-33,87], not on a belt to the labs. 4) Next time I'd hand the packs from those chests to the labs right away, then fix boiler fuel and coal delivery, and only after that build logistic science. 5) I wouldn't report research as running before the labs show packs being used."], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
