gap), the old base and iron fields are still out of fuel, and green science doesn't exist yet."], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
{"run": "20261020-001138-t-steel-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-steel", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.234, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 35, "obj_secs": {"steel": 302}, "think_min": 1.0, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 0, "looks": 17, "extra_looks": 9, "waste": 0.314, "cost_per_met": 0.234, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1], ["FAILED cannot place stone-furnace at N,N: blocked by stone-furnace@N,N, burner-mining-dril", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot place stone-furnace at N,N: blocked by stone-furnace@N,N, burner-mining-dril", "error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 1.3, "hand building": 0.43, "crafting/fetching": 0.34, "failed calls": 0.31, "walking": 0.22, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.98}, "by_tool": {"act": 8, "inspect": 8, "say": 6, "find": 6, "look": 2, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to gathering materials. I started with 8 plates and no inserters, so I walked about 60 tiles each way for stone and copper. 2) Missing: a stock chest of inserters, poles and furnaces, or a way to see what chests hold without walking to them. 3) Confusing: the two infinity chests feeding the belt weren't labeled as a source. A burner furnace at the copper patch already held 66 copper plates, which saved me a smelting step. 4) Minor: placing poles needed wood, and my first batch of 4 only crafted 1. 5) Next time: check the inventory first and craft all the intermediates in one batch. I'd also put a provider chest with spare inserters and poles near the steel row. Steel now measures 16/min."], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
{"run": "20261020-001419-t-starved-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-starved", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.212, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 32, "obj_secs": {"red-running": 120}, "think_min": 0.8, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 1, "looks": 12, "extra_looks": 5, "waste": 0.188, "cost_per_met": 0.212, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "production", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"crafting/fetching": 0.78, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "waiting on jobs": 0.27, "walking": 0.16, "hand building": 0.05, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.83}, "by_tool": {"say": 7, "act": 6, "wait": 5, "look": 4, "inspect": 4, "find": 3, "techs": 2, "production": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/4: Most time went on tracing the problem. The red science site was about 50 tiles from spawn, the only labs I found were 78 tiles away, and the output had no path at all. Walking and building the lab line took the rest.", "2/4: Missing: a way to see how the existing build was meant to work (where packs were supposed to go), and a quick map of belt directions. Each `look` was centered on me, not on the coordinates I passed, which cost a round trip.", "3/4: Confused/failed: the first fix, a belt tile facing the wrong way, only partly explained the stall. The assemblers had no output inserters, and I found that only after the first fix. I never got to the coal, boiler and furnace fuel alerts. Those are likely why iron fell to 22/min and copper is 0.", "4/4: Next time I'd check the whole chain (inputs, machines, output, consumer) before the first fix, and handle the power and fuel alerts first, since they block everything else. I'd also post a board task up front."], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
{"run": "20261020-001706-t-deliver-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-deliver", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.138, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 1.0, "calls": 22, "obj_secs": {"chest-filled": 60}, "think_min": 0.5, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 7, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.227, "cost_per_met": 0.138, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:take", "board", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "production", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.15, "waiting on jobs": 0.11, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 0.5}, "by_tool": {"say": 8, "look": 3, "act": 3, "inspect": 2, "board": 1, "marks": 1, "find": 1, "production": 1, "techs": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to finding where stock lived. A big inspect of the chest area showed the inserters and belts, so the delivery itself was one batch.", "2) I was missing a stock summary by item, and a way to find which chest holds an item. The find tool doesn't search chest contents, and my first search for iron-plate failed because that isn't an entity name.", "3) Confusing: after the delivery finished I kept getting the same order repeated, so I replied twice that it was done. Also the alerts about 32 unfueled machines at [gps=74,69] pointed far from the base, and I never got there.", "4) Next time: put the order on the board with a done_when check before starting, and fix the power and fuel alerts before the delivery. Labs are still idle because the science assembler gets no iron, and the boiler coal I added by hand is only a stopgap."], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
{"run": "20261020-001011-t-steel-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-steel", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.224, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 7.1, "calls": 28, "obj_secs": {"steel": 422}, "think_min": 1.1, "idle_min": 0.7, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 11, "extra_looks": 6, "waste": 0.214, "cost_per_met": 0.224, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 2.96, "hand building": 1.06, "idle (nothing running)": 0.67, "walking": 0.23, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.07}, "by_tool": {"act": 7, "inspect": 5, "wait": 5, "say": 4, "look": 3, "find": 2, "techs": 1, "map": 1}, "debrief": [], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
{"run": "20261020-001542-t-brownout-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-brownout", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.248, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 35, "obj_secs": {"power-steady": 241}, "think_min": 0.8, "idle_min": 0.4, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 0, "looks": 18, "extra_looks": 8, "waste": 0.286, "cost_per_met": 0.248, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot craft steam-engine: missing ingredients", 1], ["FAILED no steam-engine in inventory", 1], ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1], ["FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", "FAILED cannot craft steam-engine: missing ingredients", "FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory", "FAILED no steam-engine in inventory"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "recipes", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.39, "hand building": 0.28, "walking": 0.28, "failed calls": 0.01, "looking": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.84}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 8, "act": 7, "say": 5, "look": 4, "diagnose": 4, "find": 2, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "recipes": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on walking: I fetched 20 plates from a chest about 65 tiles away, then came back. 2) I was missing copper or poles in my inventory. I had to pull a pole from elsewhere to connect the new engine, and the steam-engine recipe needed 2 more plates than I expected. 3) Confusing: the same ops message came in twice and I wasn't sure it meant the engine rig, so I also hand-fed the other plant's boiler, which is only a stopgap. 4) Diagnose and inspect pointed straight at the cause (8 assemblers on 1 engine), which was quick. 5) Next time I'd check recipe costs with the recipes tool before walking, carry spare poles and plates, and ask which site was meant before touching the second one."], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
{"run": "20261020-001840-t-deliver-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-deliver", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.194, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 1.0, "calls": 31, "obj_secs": {"chest-filled": 60}, "think_min": 0.6, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 10, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.097, "cost_per_met": 0.194, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:research", "act:take", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait", "work"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.4, "idle (nothing running)": 0.27, "waiting on jobs": 0.17, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.58}, "by_tool": {"say": 9, "act": 7, "look": 4, "inspect": 4, "wait": 2, "work": 1, "marks": 1, "find": 1, "techs": 1, "diagnose": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: most time went on tracing how the science chain is fed. Its chests and inserters sit scattered around [gps=-20,-33], and I found them one inspect at a time.", "Missing: a map of what feeds what, plus a way to see which chest feeds an assembler. I also didn't know up front that the stock chests held the inserters and belts, so I nearly started crafting them.", "Confused me: my first batched act failed on an invalid op (inspect isn't an act op), and its first moves were still partly queued. Also the \"by\" field and alerts were hard to match to real causes.", "Honest status: research is not fixed. Red science is hand-fed and only 2 packs made. Labs are still starved: no logistic packs in one, no automation packs in the other. The far furnaces still have no fuel.", "Next time: run work and marks first, then read the whole base once and write a feeds-what note. Then I'd fix the root cause (a belt for plates and coal) instead of stocking chests by hand."], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
{"run": "20261020-001956-d4-library-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "d4-library", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.126, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 1.0, "calls": 16, "obj_secs": {"two-more-smelters": 60}, "think_min": 0.3, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 6, "extra_looks": 2, "waste": 0.125, "cost_per_met": 0.126, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:take", "build", "find", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "stamp", "techs"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.68, "hand building": 0.14, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.28}, "by_tool": {"say": 4, "inspect": 3, "stamp": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "find_space": 1, "marks": 1, "build": 1, "find": 1, "act": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) The stamp and build of both smelters took about 40s. The longest stretch was my inspect on a 14-tile radius, which dumped about 100 belt and inserter entries. 2) I had no inventory, but build fetched the belts, inserters and coal itself, so materials weren't a problem. 3) I couldn't tell whether the pole chain reached the grid. Poles always show energy 0, so I judged by the inserters, which showed energy. A grid-connected check would have helped. 4) The ore and coal supply is the missing piece. Coal is about 84 tiles away, and the boilers and furnaces are all hand-fed, so I only patched one boiler by hand. 5) Next time I'd check boiler and fuel alerts and the power chain before stamping, and use a small inspect radius."], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
{"run": "20261020-001949-d4-library-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "d4-library", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.09, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 11, "obj_secs": {"two-more-smelters": 121}, "think_min": 0.2, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 3, "extra_looks": 0, "waste": 0.0, "cost_per_met": 0.09, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["build", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "say", "techs"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.93, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.2}, "by_tool": {"say": 5, "build": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "find_space": 1, "inspect": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: the stamps took the most time, about 30s each. The second one returned \"paused\" with 0 ghosts left, so I had to check by hand that it was fully built.", "Missing: a quick way to see whether a build is powered and connected. My inspect call dumped about 100 entities when I only needed pole energy. I also never confirmed the stamps link to the grid. I inferred it from pole spacing.", "What confused me: the grid was dead (boiler out of fuel at [gps=-31,-43]), so the smelters read 0 energy and I couldn't verify them. Next time I'd fuel the boiler first, then stamp and check that the furnaces and inserters actually power up."], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
