ry", "FAILED no machine at N,N", "FAILED no path to N,N (blocked by water/cliffs/buildings?)", "FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory", "FAILED nothing to take from stone-furnace (iron-plate) (it holds N coal); nearest with iro", "FAILED nothing to take from stone-furnace (iron-plate) (it holds N coal, N iron-ore); near", "FAILED nothing to take from stone-furnace (iron-plate) (it holds N coal, N iron-plate); ne", "FAILED nothing to take from stone-furnace (iron-plate) (it holds N iron-ore); nearest with", "FAILED nothing to take from stone-furnace (iron-plate) (it holds N iron-ore, N iron-plate)", "FAILED nothing to take from stone-furnace (iron-plate) (it holds N iron-plate); nearest wi", "FAILED nothing to take from stone-furnace (iron-plate) (it holds nothing); nearest with ir", "FAILED nothing to take from stone-furnace (it holds N iron-ore, N iron-plate)", "FAILED route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and not the ingredients to craft N)", "FAILED stone-furnace won't accept coal (fuel slot already holds", "FAILED this line would feed into someone's belt at N,N; pick another end point, or pass jo", "exception: line failed after N leg(s): can't route transport-belt: no route found within s", "exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", "exception: stuck with N ghosts left: ghosts I can't build (unreachable, or blocked by some"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:blueprint", "act:build_ghosts", "act:clear_ghosts", "act:configure", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:loot", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "act:wait", "board", "build", "designs", "diagnose", "find", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "map", "mark", "marks", "notes", "post_task", "production", "say", "stamp", "stop", "techs", "update_task", "wait", "work", "zone"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 14.69, "hand building": 4.66, "blueprint/line building": 4.43, "walking": 2.87, "failed calls": 2.47, "waiting on jobs": 1.99, "crafting/fetching": 1.35, "looking": 0.03, "other": 0.01, "thinking": 24.38}, "by_tool": {"act": 116, "inspect": 76, "wait": 61, "map": 31, "look": 25, "find": 15, "say": 15, "build": 15, "diagnose": 14, "production": 6, "stamp": 6, "techs": 5}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to waiting on hand-crafting 6 labs (circuits from raw plates took ~6 min) and on the 2-minute check windows. 2) Missing: a quick lab-chain status and a \"why is this entity unpowered\" tool; the green block's only fault was one unpowered assembler, which I found by reading raw inspect dumps. 3) Confusing: the fuel alert counts dead burner drills as outages, and the pole \"energy\":0 field misled me into thinking everything was unpowered. 4) Unverified: I added 6 labs at [gps=53,33] to [gps=53,53] but stopped before seeing them all fed; the daisy-chain passes packs slowly, so the far ones may stay starved. 5) Next time: craft intermediates (circuits) in an assembler beforehand and check consumption rate (labs x research time) before assuming supply was the limit."], "phase": "train-3", "cycle": 3}
{"run": "20261020-005423-t-cross-bus-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-cross-bus", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.215, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 29, "obj_secs": {"copper-across-bus": 181}, "think_min": 0.8, "idle_min": 0.2, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 0, "looks": 15, "extra_looks": 5, "waste": 0.241, "cost_per_met": 0.215, "top_failures": [["FAILED no underground-belt in inventory", 2], ["FAILED route needs N transport-belt but you have N (and not the ingredients to craft N)", 1], ["FAILED nothing to take from iron-chest (inserter) (it holds N inserter); nearest with inse", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED no underground-belt in inventory", "FAILED nothing to take from iron-chest (inserter) (it holds N inserter); nearest with inse", "FAILED route needs N transport-belt but you have N (and not the ingredients to craft N)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.35, "waiting on jobs": 0.29, "idle (nothing running)": 0.23, "failed calls": 0.07, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.83}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 9, "act": 5, "say": 4, "look": 3, "wait": 3, "map": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "find": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on gathering materials. I started with an empty inventory and had to walk to the depot at [gps=-12,-28] for belts and undergrounds. 2) I was missing an item list for the shared chests up front, plus the bus width at the crossing. I had to read the map to count the 4 bus tiles for the underground. 3) The connect tool routed the belt along y=81 and left a gap after the underground exit. I fixed that with one extra belt tile, but I should have checked the exit tile myself. 4) The repeated 'inserter is set up' messages confused me. They described what I had already built, and I re-checked the chest each time (60 copper plates at the end). 5) Next time I'd check the depot and the exact path before placing anything, then verify delivery once. I'd also flag the unfueled boilers and idle labs sooner. I fueled the boilers by hand, which is only a stopgap."], "phase": "train-4", "cycle": 4}
{"run": "20261020-005423-t-belt-ore-sonnet-i1", "scenario": "t-belt-ore", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.227, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 34, "obj_secs": {"ore-to-furnaces": 181}, "think_min": 1.1, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 0, "looks": 18, "extra_looks": 9, "waste": 0.324, "cost_per_met": 0.227, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1], ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", "exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.35, "blueprint/line building": 0.27, "waiting on jobs": 0.2, "failed calls": 0.08, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.09}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 11, "say": 7, "act": 4, "map": 3, "find": 3, "build": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to getting materials, because I started with 8 plates and had to find the spawn depot chests for belts and undergrounds. 2) I was missing a stock overview. A \"what's in shared chests\" tool would have saved several lookups.", "3) The belt tool's endpoints confused me. It ended one row off the ore belt and one tile short of the furnace feed, so I patched two joins by hand and checked with inspect. 4) Next time I'd inspect both belt ends before calling the line tool, and look for the depot before trying to craft."], "phase": "train-4", "cycle": 4}
{"run": "20261020-005423-t-cross-bus-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-cross-bus", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.203, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 35, "obj_secs": {"copper-across-bus": 181}, "think_min": 0.7, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 1, "looks": 17, "extra_looks": 6, "waste": 0.257, "cost_per_met": 0.203, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1], ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", "exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "stop", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "blueprint/line building": 0.32, "hand building": 0.24, "waiting on jobs": 0.22, "failed calls": 0.08, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.74}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 11, "say": 7, "act": 4, "find": 3, "look": 2, "build": 2, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "stop": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on finding materials. I started with almost nothing, and the build tool's first run teleported me to the stock chests at [gps=-11,-27], where I took belts and undergrounds. 2) Missing: a way to see which shared chests hold what without walking up to them, and the foreman's checks, since \"not done yet\" came with no reason. 3) Confusing: the line tool left the last belt pointing north at [gps=-12,81], one tile past the inserter pickup. I only noticed it by inspecting, then fixed it. 4) Also repeated: I answered the same \"inserter is set up\" message twice. 5) Next time: after any belt build I'd check the last tile's direction and the chest count at once, and I'd fuel the boilers before starting, because a dry boiler slowed the flow."], "phase": "train-4", "cycle": 4}
