{"run": "20261020-010321-t-steel-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-steel", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.175, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 24, "obj_secs": {"steel": 241}, "think_min": 1.0, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 10, "extra_looks": 5, "waste": 0.208, "cost_per_met": 0.175, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "production", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 0.63, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "walking": 0.23, "hand building": 0.17, "crafting/fetching": 0.04, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.01}, "by_tool": {"say": 5, "act": 4, "inspect": 4, "wait": 3, "look": 2, "find": 2, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "production": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to the 120-tile round trip for stone, because I joined with an empty inventory and no stone or copper nearby. 2) I was missing copper (so no electric inserters) and any shared stock chest; the only chests I found were empty. 3) Nothing failed. The build worked first try, and burner inserters fed from the belt turned out to be a good copper-free workaround. 4) The output burner inserters were hand-fueled with 3 coal each, which is a stopgap, and I never put the order on the board. Steel measured 16/min at the end. 5) Next time I'd check inventory and materials before walking to the site, post the board task with a done_when first, and swap those output inserters for electric ones."], "phase": "train-4", "cycle": 4}
{"run": "20261020-010638-t-starved-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-starved", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.241, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 35, "obj_secs": {"red-running": 120}, "think_min": 1.9, "idle_min": 0.7, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 1, "looks": 14, "extra_looks": 5, "waste": 0.2, "cost_per_met": 0.241, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "post_task", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.67, "walking": 0.32, "waiting on jobs": 0.26, "failed calls": 0.24, "hand building": 0.06, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.93}, "by_tool": {"act": 9, "say": 7, "look": 6, "inspect": 3, "wait": 3, "diagnose": 2, "find": 2, "techs": 1, "post_task": 1, "map": 1}, "debrief": ["Result: red science now runs end to end. Packs go from the 3 assemblers at [gps=51,5] onto the south lane of the gear belt, then to 2 labs at [gps=63,5]. Labs are consuming packs and research is running.", "Most time: finding the real causes. The base was a half-finished scaffold: a backwards belt tile, no output inserters on the assemblers, and labs placed far from the packs.", "Missing: a quick view of the whole base layout and power grid. look only shows the area around my character, so I had to walk to see anything.", "Not solved: the steam boilers at [gps=-27,-42] are still hand-fed coal, and about 32 drills and furnaces near [gps=74,69] are out of fuel. Coal is about 85 tiles away at [gps=46,93], so it needs a belt from a coal outpost. Next time I'd trace the whole chain first and fix the power fuel before moving anything."], "phase": "train-4", "cycle": 4}
