{"run": "20261020-011206-d4-library-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "d4-library", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.066, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 1.0, "calls": 12, "obj_secs": {"two-more-smelters": 60}, "think_min": 0.2, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 4, "extra_looks": 0, "waste": 0.0, "cost_per_met": 0.066, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["build", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "say", "stamp", "zone"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.96, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.22}, "by_tool": {"say": 3, "stamp": 2, "build": 2, "inspect": 2, "look": 1, "find_space": 1, "zone": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to the 96-entity build (41s); the stamp and pole line were quick. 2) I didn't know where the grid ended. Stamps came up unpowered, and I only found that by inspecting pole energy 0. 3) The line tool placed the poles without trouble, but I only checked one inserter for power, not every machine. 4) Nothing failed, but I skipped a board task with done_when and never released the zone \"smelters\". 5) Next time I'd check grid reach first, post the task with a check, verify power on all machines, and release the zone."], "phase": "train-4", "cycle": 4}
{"run": "20261020-010734-t-starved-sonnet-i1", "scenario": "t-starved", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.372, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 57, "obj_secs": {"red-running": 120}, "think_min": 3.3, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 1, "looks": 30, "extra_looks": 19, "waste": 0.386, "cost_per_met": 0.372, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 2]], "failure_kinds": ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "post_task", "production", "recipes", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.72, "walking": 0.39, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "hand building": 0.3, "failed calls": 0.28, "crafting/fetching": 0.18, "waiting on jobs": 0.17, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 3.31}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 9, "look": 8, "say": 8, "act": 8, "find": 6, "map": 6, "build": 4, "techs": 2, "wait": 2, "post_task": 1, "production": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/4: Most time went to tracing the problem chain by hand (science block, then labs, then boilers, then coal), plus about 90 tiles of walking each way. The red science block at [gps=51,5] was one belt tile; the real blocker was power.", "2/4: I was missing a belt-trace tool that says where a belt ends, and a quick list of which item chests are infinity chests. Look and inspect always centre on me, and one inspect returned thousands of ore tiles.", "3/4: Failed or confusing: the line build first refused for lack of undergrounds, which I found in a chest. The coal belt is now laid from [gps=22,103] to [gps=-26,-40], but it's unverified. I still need an inserter from its end into the boiler chest, the second boiler at [gps=-31,-43] has no fuel feed, and the science output at 51,5 has no path to the labs.", "4/4: Next time I'd check production and power first, before touching the downstream assemblers. I'd also grab the infinity-chest gears and the undergrounds up front, and verify the belt end before laying a long line."], "phase": "train-4", "cycle": 4}
{"run": "20261020-011254-d4-library-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "d4-library", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.085, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 1.0, "calls": 15, "obj_secs": {"two-more-smelters": 60}, "think_min": 0.2, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 5, "extra_looks": 1, "waste": 0.067, "cost_per_met": 0.085, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["build", "find", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "say", "stamp"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.7, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.23}, "by_tool": {"say": 7, "look": 2, "stamp": 2, "find_space": 1, "build": 1, "find": 1, "inspect": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: the build itself was quick, 96 ghosts in 41s with the stamp. Most of my time went on checking power and fuel afterward.", "Missing: a coal supply by belt and a clear view of power status. The new furnaces were stamped with no fuel, and the ghosts ignore fuel. Also missing was any roadmap or board to say what the base needed.", "Confusing: your first message said \"two more\", but I found no existing smelter. The second message repeated the first after I'd finished, so I wasn't sure whether to rebuild. The coal find only returned a spot 85 tiles away.", "Next time: I'd confirm power and fuel before reporting done, then fix the boiler at [gps=-31.5,-43]. It has no fuel, and the coal chest next to it holds 69 coal. I'd queue research as well. I took no further actions after your stop."], "phase": "train-4", "cycle": 4}
{"run": "20261020-011030-t-brownout-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-brownout", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.216, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 33, "obj_secs": {"power-steady": 241}, "think_min": 1.2, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 16, "extra_looks": 7, "waste": 0.242, "cost_per_met": 0.216, "top_failures": [["FAILED route needs N small-electric-pole but you have N (and not the ingredients to craft ", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED route needs N small-electric-pole but you have N (and not the ingredients to craft "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "recipes", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"walking": 0.27, "waiting on jobs": 0.24, "crafting/fetching": 0.16, "hand building": 0.01, "looking": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.2}, "by_tool": {"act": 7, "look": 6, "say": 6, "inspect": 6, "find": 2, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "wait": 1, "marks": 1, "recipes": 1, "diagnose": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to walking: about 70 tiles each way to fetch plates, gears and pipes for the steam engine, then back to the site. 2) I was missing copper or a spare pole. The new engine sat unplugged until I moved an existing pole, and I had no way to craft one. 3) Confusing: the first look at [gps=0,0] showed nothing useful, and I found the site only by searching for steam-engine. The alerts also cover a lot (dead boiler, 32 unfueled furnaces, idle labs) that I only partly handled. 4) Next time I'd find the engine blocks first and check that load matches boiler and engine capacity. I'd carry spare poles and wood, and take coal for the whole base, not just one boiler. 5) Still open: the boiler at [gps=-31,-43] has no coal automation, the furnaces near [gps=74,69] are out of fuel, and no research is running."], "phase": "train-4", "cycle": 4}
