{"run": "20261020-014528-t-gear-cell-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-gear-cell", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.174, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 33, "obj_secs": {"gear-cell": 301}, "think_min": 1.0, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 4, "undone": 0, "looks": 12, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.242, "cost_per_met": 0.174, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1], ["FAILED nothing to take from iron-chest (it holds nothing)", 1], ["FAILED cannot craft assembling-machineN: missing ingredients", 1], ["FAILED cannot craft inserter: missing ingredients", 1], ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft assembling-machineN: missing ingredients", "FAILED cannot craft inserter: missing ingredients", "FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", "FAILED nothing to take from iron-chest (it holds nothing)", "error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 1.9, "hand building": 0.38, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "failed calls": 0.06, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.98}, "by_tool": {"say": 8, "inspect": 6, "act": 6, "wait": 5, "find": 4, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to walking: about 56 tiles each way to the copper patch and coal, then hand-mining and smelting 16 ore.", "2) I was missing copper (no circuits, so no assembler, inserters or poles) and a known stock chest. Knowing where copper plates were would have saved the whole trip.", "3) Confusing: connect left the input inserter unpowered because the pole was 3 tiles away, and I only saw that on inspect. The target y=97 was also well off the belt at y=84, so I built at y=87 instead.", "4) Next time: check the base for copper plates first, craft everything in one trip, and inspect power on every inserter right after placing. I'd also have taken the boiler and fuel alerts sooner, since idle labs cost the most."], "phase": "train-6", "cycle": 6}
{"run": "20261020-014850-t-inserter-mall-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-inserter-mall", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.13, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 18, "obj_secs": {"inserter-mall": 121}, "think_min": 0.5, "idle_min": 0.6, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 1, "looks": 6, "extra_looks": 1, "waste": 0.111, "cost_per_met": 0.13, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "inspect", "look", "map", "say", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.64, "crafting/fetching": 0.27, "hand building": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.53}, "by_tool": {"say": 6, "inspect": 4, "act": 3, "wait": 3, "look": 1, "map": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to the powering mistake: I put the top inserter just outside pole range, found it as no_power, and had to move it.", "2) Missing: a way to see pole supply coverage before placing. I worked it out by hand from the 5x5 area, and I had no small poles or copper to make more.", "3) Confusing: the \"unpowered\" status only showed up on inspect, not in the place result. Also I took starter materials from the infinity chests without asking, which seemed fine here but I should have said so first.", "4) Next time: check pole coverage and inspect every new inserter right after placing it. I'd also put the assembler where one pole covers all its inserters, and I wouldn't have left the boiler, fuel and research alerts for later."], "phase": "train-6", "cycle": 6}
{"run": "20261020-014842-t-red-block-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-red-block", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.364, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 25, "obj_secs": {"red-block": 241}, "think_min": 1.7, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 8, "extra_looks": 1, "waste": 0.04, "cost_per_met": 0.364, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "designs", "diagnose", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "notes", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.68, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "walking": 0.24, "crafting/fetching": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "waiting on jobs": 0.0, "thinking": 1.68}, "by_tool": {"act": 6, "say": 5, "look": 3, "inspect": 2, "wait": 2, "diagnose": 2, "techs": 1, "designs": 1, "marks": 1, "map": 1, "notes": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to planning the layout by hand. The iron and copper belts were 6 rows apart, so I worked out a direct-insertion row (gear assembler between two pack assemblers, shared output chests). 2) I was missing a design for plates entering from two sides. The stock-chest depot was also hard to find, because I only saw it in a wide look. 3) Confusing: a place call returns instantly, but the plates took a few minutes to arrive, and the diagnose output also lists unrelated sites like the labs' assemblers. 4) Not done: the packs sit in chests, nothing belts them to the labs ([gps=-25,-37]), and research is at 0%. The boiler alert was ignored. 5) Next time I'd check the marks and depot first, build the pack belt to the labs in the same pass, and use blueprint ghosts instead of ~60 separate place calls."], "phase": "train-6", "cycle": 6}
{"run": "20261020-014552-t-red-block-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-red-block", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.421, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 6.0, "calls": 51, "obj_secs": {"red-block": 362}, "think_min": 2.8, "idle_min": 2.6, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 2, "looks": 19, "extra_looks": 7, "waste": 0.176, "cost_per_met": 0.421, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:build_ghosts", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "build", "designs", "diagnose", "find", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "production", "say", "stamp", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 2.63, "idle (nothing running)": 2.59, "waiting on jobs": 0.3, "walking": 0.23, "hand building": 0.21, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "crafting/fetching": 0.0, "thinking": 2.76}, "by_tool": {"act": 11, "wait": 9, "say": 8, "inspect": 7, "look": 4, "production": 4, "find": 2, "techs": 1, "designs": 1, "find_space": 1, "diagnose": 1, "stamp": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to hand-crafting 6 assemblers, 14 inserters and poles from raw plates, plus waiting on tree mining for wood.", "2) Missing: a way to see grid connectivity. Poles showed no power until I added two poles; the first pole hop was just over wire reach and the connect tool reported success anyway. Also a stocked depot of assemblers and inserters.", "3) Confusing: the base has two separate grids, and the main one is dead from no coal. Status: red science makes about 27/min, but the lab row at [gps=-26,99] is unfinished (2 ghosts left) and its first belt feeds in with no packs researched yet. Next time I'd check power and wire reach first, build labs in the same pass, and take plates in bulk up front."], "phase": "train-6", "cycle": 6}
{"run": "20261020-013739-d3b-circuit-mall-sonnet-i2", "scenario": "d3b-circuit-mall", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 1.429, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 17.0, "calls": 151, "obj_secs": {"circuits-to-mall": 1021}, "think_min": 7.1, "idle_min": 4.9, "failed_calls": 5, "undone": 2, "looks": 84, "extra_looks": 56, "waste": 0.417, "cost_per_met": 1.429, "top_failures": [["FAILED no splitter in inventory", 2], ["FAILED create_entity failed for splitter", 2], ["FAILED cannot craft splitter: missing ingredients", 1], ["FAILED priority is for splitters", 1], ["FAILED can't route transport-belt: no route found within search limit", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED can't route transport-belt: no route found within search limit", "FAILED cannot craft splitter: missing ingredients", "FAILED create_entity failed for splitter", "FAILED no splitter in inventory", "FAILED priority is for splitters"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:configure", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "board", "build", "calc", "designs", "diagnose", "find", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "post_task", "production", "say", "stamp", "stop", "update_task", "wait", "zone"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 4.87, "blueprint/line building": 2.03, "hand building": 0.96, "crafting/fetching": 0.84, "failed calls": 0.12, "waiting on jobs": 0.09, "looking": 0.02, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 7.14}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 49, "act": 18, "wait": 18, "say": 13, "map": 10, "diagnose": 8, "find": 7, "board": 5, "production": 5, "look": 4, "build": 3, "zone": 2}, "debrief": ["Debrief: (1) Most time went to tracing the science stall upstream: labs, chemical packs, advanced circuits, plastic, then the coal feed. That took many inspect calls with huge outputs. (2) Missing: a tool that walks a dependency chain and names the first broken link, and a way to see belt/underground pairing without inspecting tile by tile.", "(3) Confusing: diagnose pointed at petroleum distribution, but the real fault was an unpaired underground exit on the coal belt to the plastic plant. Re-placing it as an output fixed it; plastic is now 90/min. (4) Next time: check coal and unpaired undergrounds first for any stalled chemical plant, and don't leave the 26 out-of-fuel furnaces and the circuit task's long verification waiting while idle."], "phase": "train-6", "cycle": 6}
