{"run": "20261020-015523-t-starved-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-starved", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.226, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 30, "obj_secs": {"red-running": 120}, "think_min": 1.3, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 1, "looks": 11, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.167, "cost_per_met": 0.226, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "post_task", "production", "say", "techs", "update_task", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 0.86, "hand building": 0.28, "walking": 0.16, "crafting/fetching": 0.1, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 1.31}, "by_tool": {"say": 8, "act": 7, "look": 4, "inspect": 4, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "find": 1, "post_task": 1, "wait": 1, "production": 1, "update_task": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/4: Most time went to working out the layout, since the science block had no output path or labs. The long walk to pick up the labs at [gps=-20,-37] cost the rest.", "Debrief 2/4: I was missing iron plates in my inventory (I only had 8, so I used chest gears and copper), and a clear map of which power network each site is on. The first lab inspect gave no hint that the labs were far away.", "Debrief 3/4: Two things tripped me. I queued research-speed-1 without checking it needs logistic packs. The board check with scope base also rejected my task with \"needs a zone\", so the task is stuck in verifying.", "Debrief 4/4: Next time I'd run `techs` and check pack types before queueing research. I'd also post the task with a zone in the done_when, and gather all parts (inserters, poles, belts) before the first walk."], "phase": "train-6", "cycle": 6}
{"run": "20261020-015625-t-starved-sonnet-i2", "scenario": "t-starved", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.24, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 34, "obj_secs": {"red-running": 120}, "think_min": 1.5, "idle_min": 0.7, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 1, "looks": 12, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.118, "cost_per_met": 0.24, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "say", "stop", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.67, "walking": 0.35, "waiting on jobs": 0.21, "crafting/fetching": 0.17, "hand building": 0.05, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.55}, "by_tool": {"say": 8, "act": 8, "inspect": 6, "look": 4, "wait": 4, "techs": 1, "find": 1, "map": 1, "stop": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/4: Most time went on working out why the labs were idle. The belt fix was quick. The real gap was that the science assemblers had no output inserters and the labs sat 80 tiles away at the old hand-fed spot.", "2/4: I was missing a base overview. I only found the labs, and that the alerts were about a different setup, by wandering with find and look. The techs list also doesn't flag which techs need green science until you read the pack lists. I queued research-speed-1 first and it couldn't run.", "3/4: What confused me was the old chest-fed lab area, which looked half-built and abandoned (I took its labs, 2 inserters and 2 poles without asking). Also, the inspect results showed lab status as missing_science_packs while it held packs, which was really a research-queue problem.", "4/4: Next time I'd call the board and look at the whole map first and trace science from pack to lab before touching anything, and ask before pulling parts from the old build. I'd also check pack requirements before queueing research. Open items: the green science build, plus coal and power at [gps=-31,-43] and [gps=74,69]. I haven't measured research output, only that both labs show as working."], "phase": "train-6", "cycle": 6}
{"run": "20261020-015829-t-deliver-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-deliver", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.147, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 1.0, "calls": 25, "obj_secs": {"chest-filled": 60}, "think_min": 0.5, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 9, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.2, "cost_per_met": 0.147, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:research", "act:take", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"crafting/fetching": 0.48, "hand building": 0.19, "waiting on jobs": 0.18, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 0.45}, "by_tool": {"say": 7, "act": 5, "find": 4, "look": 3, "marks": 2, "inspect": 2, "techs": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/4: Most time went to finding materials. I started with 8 plates and no marks, so I had to inspect chests to find the stock depot around [gps=-12,-29].", "2/4: I was missing a stock list. A single call showing chest contents would have saved several calls. Nobody had marked the depot chests.", "3/4: I misread craft count. count=50 on transport-belt gave 100 belts (50 crafts), which wasted about 50 iron plates. The big look and inspect outputs were also very long.", "4/4: Next time I'd check the depot chests before crafting anything. I'd also have taken the inserters from stock first and mark the depot. I left the fuel outages at [gps=74,69] and science production unfixed."], "phase": "train-6", "cycle": 6}
{"run": "20261020-015957-t-deliver-sonnet-i2", "scenario": "t-deliver", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.132, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 1.0, "calls": 19, "obj_secs": {"chest-filled": 60}, "think_min": 0.4, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 8, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.211, "cost_per_met": 0.132, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:take", "board", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 0.2, "hand building": 0.16, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.45}, "by_tool": {"say": 4, "look": 3, "find": 3, "act": 3, "inspect": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "board": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on finding where stock was. I started with an empty inventory and had to inspect around to find the depot chests near [gps=-12,-29]; after that the delivery took two calls. 2) Missing: a one-call \"what's in the shared chests\" view. marks showed nothing, so I scanned by hand. 3) Confusing: the order was already done when the \"take or craft\" follow-up came, and my first acts return said \"still running\" while the second showed the finished moves. 4) The alerts were real but not fixed: the boilers only got a hand-fed coal stopgap, and the 32 out-of-fuel machines out east, no science and no copper were left untouched. 5) Next time I'd mark the depot chests as providers on arrival and put a coal belt to the boilers on the board straight away."], "phase": "train-6", "cycle": 6}
{"run": "20261020-015256-t-steel-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-steel", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.21, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 6.0, "calls": 25, "obj_secs": {"steel": 362}, "think_min": 1.3, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 9, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.16, "cost_per_met": 0.21, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 2.36, "crafting/fetching": 0.38, "hand building": 0.24, "walking": 0.22, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.26}, "by_tool": {"act": 9, "look": 3, "say": 3, "inspect": 3, "find": 2, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": [], "phase": "train-6", "cycle": 6}
{"run": "20261020-020001-d4-library-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "d4-library", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.079, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 11, "obj_secs": {"two-more-smelters": 121}, "think_min": 0.5, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 3, "extra_looks": 0, "waste": 0.0, "cost_per_met": 0.079, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "build", "find_space", "look", "say", "stop", "techs"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.93, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "hand building": 0.0, "thinking": 0.47}, "by_tool": {"say": 3, "look": 2, "build": 2, "techs": 1, "find_space": 1, "act": 1, "stop": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to the two stamps (about 30s each); the build tool did all the fetching and crafting, so it was cheap for me. 2) I was missing a way to confirm power directly: I only inferred it from the inserters showing waiting_for_source_items instead of a power fault. 3) Confusing: your \"stop building\" order came while I was walking to the boiler. I stopped that job, so the boiler at [gps=-31.5,-43] is still unfueled. Also, I answered a repeat of an order I'd already finished. 4) Next time: check the board and chat history before re-answering, and report a coal/fuel plan alongside new furnaces."], "phase": "train-6", "cycle": 6}
{"run": "20261020-015640-t-brownout-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-brownout", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.661, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 72, "obj_secs": {"power-steady": 241}, "think_min": 2.4, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 3, "undone": 1, "looks": 41, "extra_looks": 28, "waste": 0.444, "cost_per_met": 0.661, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot craft steam-engine: missing ingredients", 1], ["FAILED no steam-engine in inventory", 1], ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", 1], ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1], ["FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", "FAILED cannot craft steam-engine: missing ingredients", "FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory", "FAILED no steam-engine in inventory", "error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "designs", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "post_task", "say", "skill_read", "stop", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 1.52, "waiting on jobs": 1.3, "failed calls": 0.1, "looking": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "own scripts": 0.0, "thinking": 2.43}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 20, "say": 11, "act": 10, "map": 9, "find": 7, "wait": 5, "diagnose": 3, "look": 2, "techs": 1, "designs": 1, "post_task": 1, "skill_read": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to tracing why science was starved: the belt-fed chain was broken at [gps=71,-25] and copper ore piles up at a dead-end belt [gps=0,79] with no smelter.", "2) Missing: a belt-tracing tool (follow belt to end, show lane contents) and a plate/stock list per chest; I had to inspect tile by tile and walk 100+ tiles for 2 iron plates. Crafting 150 belts also took ~3 min of real time.", "3) Confusing: repeated \"your call\" replies with no answer; craft count semantics (queued far more belts than asked). Fixed: 2nd steam engine at the south site and the iron belt turn. NOT done: copper smelter (stamp smelting-column-12 at [gps=-5,67] on the ore belt end, coal via belt joined at [gps=22,102]) and the copper plate belt to science.", "4) Next time: stamp the smelter first with a pre-stocked chest of materials, and check belt ends before building anything new."], "phase": "train-6", "cycle": 6}
