{"run": "20261020-020626-t-cross-bus-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-cross-bus", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.133, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 21, "obj_secs": {"copper-across-bus": 181}, "think_min": 0.5, "idle_min": 0.5, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 10, "extra_looks": 2, "waste": 0.143, "cost_per_met": 0.133, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:take", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.46, "blueprint/line building": 0.32, "failed calls": 0.08, "hand building": 0.01, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.54}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 6, "say": 4, "look": 2, "build": 2, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "find": 1, "act": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to checking where the belt ended and finding belt and underground materials; the stock chests near [gps=-11,-27] had them. 2) I was missing the inserter's real pickup tile (the map arrows were ambiguous) and a quick way to see what's in the stock chests. 3) Confusing: the first build failed on missing undergrounds, and the second call walked me to the stock chests and fetched belts on its own. I also repeated the same status report after you'd already said it was done. 4) Next time I'd inspect the inserter first, grab undergrounds up front, and verify with one chest check instead of several waits. Boiler fuel and idle labs are still unaddressed."], "phase": "train-7", "cycle": 7}
{"run": "20261020-020626-t-belt-ore-sonnet-i2", "scenario": "t-belt-ore", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.182, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 26, "obj_secs": {"ore-to-furnaces": 241}, "think_min": 0.8, "idle_min": 0.7, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 13, "extra_looks": 6, "waste": 0.269, "cost_per_met": 0.182, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.67, "blueprint/line building": 0.27, "failed calls": 0.22, "walking": 0.21, "hand building": 0.1, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.79}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 6, "act": 4, "say": 4, "look": 3, "find": 2, "map": 2, "build": 2, "wait": 2, "techs": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to walking about 100 tiles each way to the base chests for belts and undergrounds, because I started with almost nothing. 2) The build line reported \"done\", but ore didn't flow because the drill belt ended one tile short of my line's start. I only found that by inspecting the belts. 3) I was missing a clear belt-end and flow check from the tools, and a stock of belts and undergrounds in my inventory. 4) Next time I'll inspect both belt ends before running the line, carry spare belts, and check for ore on the belt right after building. 5) I never got to the boiler fuel, the dead furnaces or research."], "phase": "train-7", "cycle": 7}
