{"run": "20261020-021105-t-gear-cell-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-gear-cell", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.244, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 33, "obj_secs": {"gear-cell": 241}, "think_min": 1.3, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 17, "extra_looks": 7, "waste": 0.242, "cost_per_met": 0.244, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called chest (did you mean wooden-chest, iron-chest, steel-chest, active-", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called chest (did you mean wooden-chest, iron-chest, steel-chest, active-"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "act:wait", "designs", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "stop", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.45, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "crafting/fetching": 0.08, "waiting on jobs": 0.01, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 1.34}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 9, "find": 5, "act": 5, "say": 4, "look": 2, "marks": 2, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "designs": 1, "stop": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on the ~110-tile walk to the stock chests at the spawn base, because I started with almost nothing in my inventory. 2) I was missing a list of where shared stock was; I only found it by scanning with look. 3) The output inserter had no power at first, since I forgot a small pole covers only a 5x5 area. 4) I placed the build at y=87 to y=90 instead of the [gps=-34,97] you named, because I tapped the belt directly, and I should have said so up front. 5) Next time: check the shared chests first, then place poles so they cover every inserter, and report the real gear count once it passes the target."], "phase": "train-7", "cycle": 7}
{"run": "20261020-020843-t-smelter-column-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-smelter-column", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.387, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 6.0, "calls": 47, "obj_secs": {"eight-furnaces": 362}, "think_min": 2.3, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 18, "looks": 15, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.489, "cost_per_met": 0.387, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:blueprint", "act:build_ghosts", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "designs", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "production", "say", "techs", "wait", "work"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 1.55, "hand building": 0.42, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "failed calls": 0.17, "waiting on jobs": 0.04, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 2.32}, "by_tool": {"act": 11, "say": 10, "look": 7, "build": 5, "inspect": 4, "techs": 2, "map": 2, "designs": 1, "wait": 1, "marks": 1, "find": 1, "work": 1}, "debrief": ["Most time went to reading big look dumps and walking about 100 tiles to the boiler, for a small fix. I was missing a clear goal or roadmap, plus any copper or science status, so I guessed at what mattered.", "What confused me: the alerts said 32 furnaces and drills out of fuel and 1 boiler dry, but only the boiler was a quick fix. The research queue also accepted a tech the labs can't run (no packs, no copper).", "Next time I'd check production first and go straight to the root cause, copper to science packs, instead of hand-fueling a boiler. I'd also put the work on the board as a task, with a coal belt to the boilers as the real fix."], "phase": "train-7", "cycle": 7}
