{"run": "20261020-021204-t-red-block-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-red-block", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.281, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 30, "obj_secs": {"red-block": 301}, "think_min": 1.9, "idle_min": 0.6, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 7, "extra_looks": 2, "waste": 0.1, "cost_per_met": 0.281, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot craft iron-chest: missing ingredients", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft iron-chest: missing ingredients"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "act:wait", "designs", "inspect", "look", "map", "mark", "marks", "production", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.58, "waiting on jobs": 0.56, "walking": 0.23, "crafting/fetching": 0.05, "hand building": 0.01, "failed calls": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.87}, "by_tool": {"say": 8, "act": 7, "inspect": 4, "wait": 4, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "designs": 1, "marks": 1, "map": 1, "mark": 1, "production": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: most time went to hand-crafting assemblers, inserters and poles, plus waiting on the supply chest for plates and mining wood for poles.", "Missing: starter stock of assemblers, inserters and poles, and the lab positions, which I never found so the packs sit in chests. The red-science-5 design needed gears and copper on one belt, which didn't match two separate belts, so I laid out my own.", "Confusing: my first craft only queued 4 of 6 assemblers because iron ran out, and I misjudged the output (I wrote 0.3/s, which is 18/min). Also a move result showed me at x=-20 mid-walk.", "Next time: check the inventory against the whole build before crafting, build the pack belt to the labs in the same job instead of ending at chests, and use a stamp or copy for the second group."], "phase": "train-7", "cycle": 7}
{"run": "20261020-021517-t-inserter-mall-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-inserter-mall", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.119, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 13, "obj_secs": {"inserter-mall": 121}, "think_min": 0.5, "idle_min": 0.6, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 5, "extra_looks": 1, "waste": 0.154, "cost_per_met": 0.119, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "inspect", "look", "map", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.58, "failed calls": 0.27, "hand building": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.52}, "by_tool": {"say": 3, "inspect": 3, "act": 2, "wait": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "map": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went into placing the assembler so every inserter sat inside existing pole coverage, because I had no copper or poles to craft new ones. 2) I was missing copper plates or a spare pole, and the map didn't show pole supply areas. 3) Nothing failed. The pole craft was refused, so I worked around it. I also pulled 60 plates, 20 gears and 20 circuits from the infinity chests, which I assumed was fine since they refill. 4) Next time I'd carry a few poles and check coverage first. I'd also set a limit on the output chest so it doesn't fill up and block the assembler."], "phase": "train-7", "cycle": 7}
{"run": "20261020-021530-t-inserter-mall-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-inserter-mall", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.137, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 17, "obj_secs": {"inserter-mall": 121}, "think_min": 0.8, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 5, "extra_looks": 1, "waste": 0.118, "cost_per_met": 0.137, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "walking": 0.22, "hand building": 0.18, "waiting on jobs": 0.1, "failed calls": 0.05, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.79}, "by_tool": {"say": 4, "act": 4, "inspect": 3, "wait": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to the power pole: I had no copper, so I walked about 140 tiles to take two spare poles from an unused line. 2) Missing: copper plates or a stock chest of poles and basic parts. 3) Confusing: I started with almost nothing and only found the infinity chests by inspecting. 4) Smaller issues: I guessed at belt rows and had to inspect to confirm them, and a failed craft cost a retry. 5) Next time: check what's in the infinity chests before crafting, and ask where spare poles are before walking to find them."], "phase": "train-7", "cycle": 7}
{"run": "20261020-020940-t-smelter-column-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-smelter-column", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.64, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 8.1, "calls": 58, "obj_secs": {"eight-furnaces": 482}, "think_min": 2.6, "idle_min": 1.3, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 60, "looks": 25, "extra_looks": 12, "waste": 1.276, "cost_per_met": 0.64, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 2]], "failure_kinds": ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "designs", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "post_task", "production", "say", "stamp", "techs", "update_task", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 1.34, "blueprint/line building": 1.33, "hand building": 0.8, "failed calls": 0.42, "waiting on jobs": 0.04, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 2.63}, "by_tool": {"act": 13, "inspect": 12, "map": 7, "build": 6, "wait": 5, "look": 4, "say": 3, "techs": 1, "post_task": 1, "marks": 1, "designs": 1, "stamp": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: Most time went to the 8-furnace iron smelting off the ore belt (walking, fueling, placing by hand). Missing: a quick way to see belt layout and ore flow without slow maps. Confusion: the base shows 0 copper, 0 science and idle labs, so iron is made but nothing consumes it. Next time: check production and research state first, then stamp a proven smelter design instead of hand-placing."], "phase": "train-7", "cycle": 7}
{"run": "20261020-021405-t-red-block-sonnet-i1", "scenario": "t-red-block", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.225, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 22, "obj_secs": {"red-block": 241}, "think_min": 1.1, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 4, "extra_looks": 0, "waste": 0.0, "cost_per_met": 0.225, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "act:wait", "designs", "diagnose", "look", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 1.73, "walking": 0.22, "crafting/fetching": 0.14, "hand building": 0.06, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.08}, "by_tool": {"act": 7, "say": 5, "wait": 4, "look": 3, "techs": 1, "designs": 1, "diagnose": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on hand-crafting 6 assemblers, 14 inserters and poles. It's slow, and the infinity chests only gave 100 plates per take, so I took several times. 2) I was missing a way to pull the build materials from the chests automatically (build kind=stamp would have needed a custom design) and a bulk craft/fetch tool. 3) Nothing failed. The only odd thing was inserter drop positions printing as e.g. -49.7 even though they landed in the right chest. 4) Next time I'd craft intermediates in the background while walking, and save this S-G-S layout as a design with copy. 5) I never got packs to the labs or queued research, so the labs are still idle."], "phase": "train-7", "cycle": 7}
{"run": "20261020-021620-t-steel-sonnet-i2", "scenario": "t-steel", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.192, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 23, "obj_secs": {"steel": 181}, "think_min": 0.7, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 0, "looks": 10, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.217, "cost_per_met": 0.192, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called rock (did you mean rocket-silo, rocket-turret, big-sand-rock, big-", 1], ["FAILED nothing minable at N,N; within N tiles: huge-rock at N,N, big-rock at N,N,", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED nothing minable at N,N; within N tiles: huge-rock at N,N, big-rock at N,N,", "error: no entity called rock (did you mean rocket-silo, rocket-turret, big-sand-rock, big-"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 0.4, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "failed calls": 0.23, "crafting/fetching": 0.21, "hand building": 0.17, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.67}, "by_tool": {"act": 5, "say": 4, "inspect": 4, "find": 3, "wait": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "diagnose": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to the 100-tile walk and sourcing materials: I spawned with almost nothing and had to mine a rock for stone, then take plates from the infinity chest. 2) Missing: copper (no electric inserters or poles, so I used burner inserters) and a starter kit in inventory. 3) Confusing: the first \"nothing minable\" on the rock coordinates, and no way to see a steel rate over time except diagnose. 4) Nothing really failed; the layout worked first try, though the hand-fueled output inserters are a stopgap. 5) Next time: check the inventory and nearby stock before leaving spawn, and put copper on the belt so the line can be fully electric."], "phase": "train-7", "cycle": 7}
{"run": "20261020-021729-t-starved-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-starved", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.264, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 37, "obj_secs": {"red-running": 120}, "think_min": 1.4, "idle_min": 0.6, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 9, "looks": 14, "extra_looks": 2, "waste": 0.297, "cost_per_met": 0.264, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "stop", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.58, "waiting on jobs": 0.51, "hand building": 0.32, "walking": 0.15, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 1.37}, "by_tool": {"act": 9, "look": 7, "say": 7, "inspect": 5, "wait": 3, "techs": 2, "find": 1, "marks": 1, "map": 1, "stop": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: most time went to the lab and inserter fix-ups: I placed the output and lab inserters facing the wrong way, and my queued rotates sat behind a leftover wait job, so I had to stop and redo them.", "Missing: a quick way to see the whole science chain's state at once, and the pickup/drop tiles shown before placing an inserter (I should have passed pickup=/drop= instead of a direction). I also queued research-speed-1 before checking it needs green science.", "Confusing: look at radius 16 centred on me, not the gps I wanted, so I had to walk there first. Next time I'll use explicit pickup=/drop= on inserters, check each rotation right after placing, and run stop before re-queuing. I haven't measured packs per minute yet."], "phase": "train-7", "cycle": 7}
{"run": "20261020-021932-t-deliver-sonnet-i2", "scenario": "t-deliver", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.171, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 1.0, "calls": 26, "obj_secs": {"chest-filled": 60}, "think_min": 0.8, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 12, "extra_looks": 6, "waste": 0.269, "cost_per_met": 0.171, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:research", "act:take", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.31, "walking": 0.16, "waiting on jobs": 0.07, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 0.77}, "by_tool": {"say": 7, "look": 4, "inspect": 4, "act": 4, "find": 3, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "diagnose": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/4: The most time went to finding stock. I walked and inspected about 20 chests to learn the depot near [gps=-13,-28] had 100 inserters and 237 belts. The delivery itself took one act call.", "2/4: I was missing a base-wide item search (for example \"where is copper-plate\") and a power status. `find` only takes entity names, and the pole energy readings showed 0 even though the labs were powered. That made me think power was down.", "3/4: Confusing: `look` radius 48 returned huge output with a lot of belt noise. I also queued research-speed-1 before noticing only 10 logistic packs exist, so I had to reorder the queue to a red-only tech.", "4/4: Next time I'd run `marks`, `production` and `diagnose` first, then take from stock and deliver straight away. The red science feed is still hand-fed and will run dry, and the 32 furnaces and drills out of coal around [gps=74,69] are still unfixed."], "phase": "train-7", "cycle": 7}
{"run": "20261020-021742-t-starved-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-starved", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.118, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 46, "obj_secs": {"red-running": 120}, "think_min": 1.8, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 1, "looks": 21, "extra_looks": 12, "waste": 0.304, "cost_per_met": 0.118, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot craft inserter: missing ingredients", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft inserter: missing ingredients"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "post_task", "production", "say", "stop", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"walking": 0.41, "waiting on jobs": 0.37, "hand building": 0.26, "crafting/fetching": 0.01, "looking": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.79}, "by_tool": {"act": 10, "say": 9, "look": 8, "find": 7, "inspect": 4, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "post_task": 1, "map": 1, "production": 1, "marks": 1, "stop": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: (1) Most time went to scouting. Coal is ~150 tiles from the boilers, and look/inspect centre on me and dump huge output, so each lookup of a far site cost a lot.", "(2) Missing: a way to see belt/power network connectivity and who feeds what, plus an inserter or poles in stock. I had 8 plates, no circuits, no copper, so even one inserter wasn't craftable. (3) Confusing: the red rig had infinity chests and a test power source, and looked like the real base. The labs at [gps=-25,-37] are a separate hand-fed site.", "(4) Status: not finished. The belt is only partly prepared: about 300 belts are crafting and I planned to replace the coal chest at [gps=42,103] with a belt run to the boilers. Fixed so far: the belt tile at [gps=46,2], the boiler fuel, and research queued. Next time I'd stock circuits, copper and poles first, then build one long belt in a single build call."], "phase": "train-7", "cycle": 7}
{"run": "20261020-021818-t-brownout-sonnet-i1", "scenario": "t-brownout", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.232, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 33, "obj_secs": {"power-steady": 241}, "think_min": 1.3, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 17, "extra_looks": 7, "waste": 0.242, "cost_per_met": 0.232, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1], ["FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", "FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "recipes", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.37, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "walking": 0.11, "waiting on jobs": 0.04, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 1.34}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 9, "act": 6, "say": 5, "look": 4, "find": 2, "wait": 2, "diagnose": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "recipes": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to walking: the plate chest was about 65 tiles from the power site, and I started with only 8 plates. 2) I was missing copper and poles; I had to pull a pole from another spot because I couldn't hand-craft one. 3) The alert text confused me: it said \"boiler out of fuel\" for a spare boiler with no feeder, so I couldn't tell what mattered. The call that the cause was 8 assemblers on 1 engine came from comparing machine counts with the engine's output. 4) Next time I'd check the starting inventory and nearby chests first, and carry spare poles and plates. I'd also leave a mark on anything I hand-fueled."], "phase": "train-7", "cycle": 7}
