{"run": "20261020-022129-d4-library-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "d4-library", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.105, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 16, "obj_secs": {"two-more-smelters": 121}, "think_min": 0.2, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 6, "extra_looks": 1, "waste": 0.062, "cost_per_met": 0.105, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:take", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "stamp", "techs"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.96, "hand building": 0.12, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.22}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 3, "say": 3, "look": 2, "stamp": 2, "build": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "find": 1, "act": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to the smelter build itself (about 44s for 96 pieces) and finding power for it; the rest was quick. 2) I started with almost nothing, so I didn't know the storage chests near [gps=-10,-27] held belts, inserters and furnaces until I looked. A mark or inventory summary would have helped.", "3) Confusing: the stamp didn't power itself, so the inserters showed no_power until I ran a pole line, and the base was in a brownout from a dead boiler. 4) Next time I'd check power and boiler fuel before building, and ask whether \"side by side\" meant east-west, since I stacked them north-south. I also left research idle and the boiler coal hand-fed, both still open."], "phase": "train-7", "cycle": 7}
