{"run": "20261020-022555-t-power-line-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-power-line", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.181, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 25, "obj_secs": {"power-the-block": 121}, "think_min": 0.5, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 12, "extra_looks": 6, "waste": 0.24, "cost_per_met": 0.181, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:take", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "status", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.64, "waiting on jobs": 0.22, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.55}, "by_tool": {"say": 6, "look": 5, "find": 4, "inspect": 3, "act": 3, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "wait": 1, "status": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: Most time went on finding poles (a shared chest at [gps=-12,-27] had 100) and walking about 130 tiles each way to the site. Missing: a way to see entities far from me; find and look only searched near me, so I couldn't confirm the assemblers existed until I got there. Confusing: look with x,y still centered on my position, and the repeated pole message made me re-answer. Next time I'd check shared chests first, then queue the pole line right away. I'd also flag the boiler and coal shortage earlier, because the power and fuel risk is still open."], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-022555-t-power-line-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-power-line", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.193, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 28, "obj_secs": {"power-the-block": 121}, "think_min": 0.5, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 9, "extra_looks": 2, "waste": 0.071, "cost_per_met": 0.193, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:take", "build", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"walking": 0.73, "blueprint/line building": 0.45, "waiting on jobs": 0.07, "hand building": 0.04, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.45}, "by_tool": {"say": 9, "look": 6, "act": 6, "techs": 1, "build": 1, "inspect": 1, "find": 1, "marks": 1, "diagnose": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: the power line was quick (one build line call, 9 poles). The fuel round took the most time, mainly walking about 150 tiles each way and about 23 separate insert actions.", "Missing: a fuel-all-in-zone action and a list of out-of-fuel machines with coordinates (I had to eyeball a look result), plus a spare stock of coal and poles on me. I started with almost nothing.", "Confusing: the first poles were already placed when the second order arrived, so I wasn't sure it was still open. look only shows entities near me, so I had to walk to a site before I could see it. I also never checked that gears came out of the assemblers.", "Next time: automate coal first (belt to the boilers and the iron field), put the work on the board, and verify output before reporting. I'd also queue research and science early so the labs never sit idle."], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-022555-t-belt-ore-sonnet-i2", "scenario": "t-belt-ore", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.239, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 33, "obj_secs": {"ore-to-furnaces": 241}, "think_min": 0.9, "idle_min": 0.9, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 14, "extra_looks": 5, "waste": 0.152, "cost_per_met": 0.239, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.9, "hand building": 0.58, "waiting on jobs": 0.23, "walking": 0.2, "crafting/fetching": 0.18, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.94}, "by_tool": {"say": 7, "act": 5, "wait": 5, "inspect": 5, "look": 4, "find": 3, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "map": 1, "diagnose": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on walking: I started at spawn with almost nothing, so the round trip to the stock chests for plates and undergrounds and then out to x=100 took longest. 2) Missing: a view of the far site from the start. `look` only showed near me, and I had to use `find` to locate drills and furnaces. 3) Confusing: `connect` is an act op, not a tool, and I called it wrong first. I also almost reported done after the belt, but the furnace output inserters sat one tile off the furnaces, so no plates left. 4) Next time: after any belt job I'd inspect the whole chain through to the output chest before reporting, and carry a belt/inserter kit when I go out."], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-022555-t-belt-ore-sonnet-i1", "scenario": "t-belt-ore", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.217, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 37, "obj_secs": {"ore-to-furnaces": 302}, "think_min": 1.5, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 18, "extra_looks": 9, "waste": 0.27, "cost_per_met": 0.217, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 1.17, "idle (nothing running)": 0.25, "failed calls": 0.22, "walking": 0.21, "crafting/fetching": 0.1, "blueprint/line building": 0.05, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.47}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 11, "say": 7, "act": 5, "wait": 4, "look": 2, "find": 2, "map": 2, "build": 2, "techs": 1, "diagnose": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/4: Most time went on the walk to base for undergrounds and plates, then hand-crafting belts. The route itself was one build call.", "Debrief 2/4: I was missing an item list for a nearby depot, and correct belt-end coordinates. The map rows are tile indices, so a belt at row -43 sits at y=-42.5, and I misread that.", "Debrief 3/4: The line tool started one tile off the old belt end and stopped one tile short of the feed belt. Both gaps only showed up when I inspected the belts, and the tool still said done. I patched them by hand.", "Debrief 4/4: Next time I'd inspect both belt endpoints before building and check ore at the furnaces straight after. I'd also flag the boiler and coal outages sooner, since they stall research."], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-022808-t-smelter-column-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-smelter-column", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.226, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 27, "obj_secs": {"eight-furnaces": 181}, "think_min": 1.1, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 12, "extra_looks": 5, "waste": 0.185, "cost_per_met": 0.226, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.6, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "waiting on jobs": 0.0, "thinking": 1.14}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 6, "act": 6, "say": 5, "find": 3, "marks": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "wait": 1, "diagnose": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to the long walk to the depot at y=-28 and back, plus the 25 placements in one queued batch. 2) I started with almost nothing and had to find the depot chests myself; a marked shared-stock list would have saved a step. 3) Confusing: the ore belt was said to carry coal but showed none, so the furnaces ran on hand-fed coal, and the pasted inserter drop reported 60.7 instead of 60.5. 4) Also 'look' isn't an act op, which wasted a call. 5) Next time I'd check belt contents (coal) before building, and start the coal feed and boiler automation in the same pass instead of hand-fuelling."], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-022555-t-cross-bus-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-cross-bus", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.162, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 25, "obj_secs": {"copper-across-bus": 181}, "think_min": 0.9, "idle_min": 0.1, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 1, "looks": 14, "extra_looks": 6, "waste": 0.36, "cost_per_met": 0.162, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1], ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", "exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 0.72, "blueprint/line building": 0.32, "failed calls": 0.08, "idle (nothing running)": 0.06, "hand building": 0.01, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.86}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 8, "find": 3, "say": 3, "look": 2, "build": 2, "act": 2, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": [], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-022823-t-smelter-column-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-smelter-column", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.24, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 30, "obj_secs": {"eight-furnaces": 181}, "think_min": 1.5, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 13, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.133, "cost_per_met": 0.24, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:clear_ghosts", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "designs", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "skill_read", "stamp", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 0.51, "hand building": 0.18, "blueprint/line building": 0.02, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "own scripts": 0.0, "thinking": 1.47}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 7, "act": 5, "say": 4, "map": 2, "marks": 2, "find": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "designs": 1, "skill_read": 1, "stamp": 1, "build": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to finding materials and working out the \"my-smelter\" stamp. Its layout was opaque, so I cleared it and hand-placed my own row. 2) I was missing a way to see a design's layout before stamping. I also didn't know the stock chests at about [gps=-12,-28] existed until I searched for containers. 3) I called the tool \"clear_ghosts\" directly and \"act\" with no prefix, and both failed. It's an act op, and the tool name is mcp__game__act. 4) The ore belt had no coal at first, so I hand-fed the furnaces. Coal showed up later, but I never watched it long enough to confirm the furnaces keep themselves fuelled. 5) Next time I'd check the stock chests first and verify belt lanes before building. I'd also post a board task at the start, which I skipped."], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-022555-t-cross-bus-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-cross-bus", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.202, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 27, "obj_secs": {"copper-across-bus": 241}, "think_min": 0.7, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 1, "looks": 14, "extra_looks": 6, "waste": 0.333, "cost_per_met": 0.202, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1], ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", "exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 0.79, "blueprint/line building": 0.42, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "crafting/fetching": 0.22, "failed calls": 0.08, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.73}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 8, "say": 4, "find": 3, "wait": 3, "map": 2, "build": 2, "act": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": [], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-023011-t-gear-cell-sonnet-i2", "scenario": "t-gear-cell", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.192, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 25, "obj_secs": {"gear-cell": 181}, "think_min": 0.6, "idle_min": 0.2, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 11, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.12, "cost_per_met": 0.192, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "recipes", "say", "wait", "work"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.56, "idle (nothing running)": 0.17, "crafting/fetching": 0.08, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.58}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 6, "act": 5, "say": 4, "look": 2, "find": 2, "wait": 2, "work": 1, "map": 1, "recipes": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on walking, about 110 tiles each way between the stock chests near [gps=-12,-28] and the belt at [gps=-40,87]. 2) I started with almost nothing in my inventory and had to find the stock chests myself. A marked depot with contents would have saved a look. 3) The output inserter had no power, because a pole 3 tiles away doesn't cover it. I only caught it by inspecting after the build, so I'll check power coverage as soon as I place things. 4) Nothing else failed, but the act tool rejected \"look\" as an action, which cost me one call. 5) Next time I'd gather everything in one trip and place the pole first. I'd also flag the dead boilers and coal-less furnaces earlier, since they leave the base at zero output."], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-023141-t-inserter-mall-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-inserter-mall", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.117, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 12, "obj_secs": {"inserter-mall": 121}, "think_min": 0.6, "idle_min": 0.2, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 4, "extra_looks": 1, "waste": 0.083, "cost_per_met": 0.117, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"crafting/fetching": 0.27, "idle (nothing running)": 0.17, "hand building": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.6}, "by_tool": {"say": 3, "inspect": 2, "act": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "map": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to working out power coverage. I had no copper for poles, so I placed the assembler so the two existing poles reached all three inserters. 2) I started with almost nothing, so I took the build materials from the infinity chests. Knowing up front that they were fair to use would have saved a look. 3) Nothing failed. I only checked output once (4 inserters in the chest) and never measured a steady rate. 4) Next time I'd put a board task with a done_when check on the order and check production before reporting. I'd also say sooner that I saw the boiler and fuel alerts but wasn't assigned them."], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-023112-t-gear-cell-sonnet-i1", "scenario": "t-gear-cell", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.156, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 27, "obj_secs": {"gear-cell": 181}, "think_min": 0.7, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 10, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.111, "cost_per_met": 0.156, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "stop", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.27, "idle (nothing running)": 0.26, "crafting/fetching": 0.08, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "waiting on jobs": 0.0, "thinking": 0.72}, "by_tool": {"say": 7, "inspect": 5, "act": 4, "find": 3, "wait": 3, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "stop": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: most time went to finding parts. I started with almost nothing and had to look for the supply chests near [gps=-12,-28] before I could build.", "Missing: a shared-stock list. A marks entry for that depot would have saved several steps. The map also doesn't show chest contents.", "What confused me: the pole chain from `connect` didn't reach the output inserter, and I only saw the no_power status after a delay. I also never measured the gear rate, so I can't say if it's slow.", "Next time I'd check pole coverage for every inserter when I place it. I'd measure the output rate before reporting. I'd also queue the supply run and the build in one batch."], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-023232-t-inserter-mall-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-inserter-mall", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.199, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 20, "obj_secs": {"inserter-mall": 121}, "think_min": 1.1, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 9, "extra_looks": 2, "waste": 0.15, "cost_per_met": 0.199, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "walking": 0.22, "crafting/fetching": 0.16, "hand building": 0.08, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "waiting on jobs": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 1.05}, "by_tool": {"act": 4, "inspect": 4, "say": 3, "find": 3, "wait": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": [], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-023427-t-starved-sonnet-i1", "scenario": "t-starved", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.262, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 33, "obj_secs": {"red-running": 120}, "think_min": 1.9, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 1, "looks": 15, "extra_looks": 8, "waste": 0.273, "cost_per_met": 0.262, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "post_task", "say", "stop", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"walking": 0.68, "waiting on jobs": 0.32, "hand building": 0.31, "idle (nothing running)": 0.25, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.88}, "by_tool": {"act": 9, "look": 8, "say": 5, "find": 3, "inspect": 2, "techs": 1, "diagnose": 1, "post_task": 1, "wait": 1, "map": 1, "stop": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to scouting. The base is spread out, and look/map ignore x,y centers, so I had to walk to see anything. 2) I was missing a map of what's connected to what. I couldn't tell the chest-fed boilers, the burner iron field and the infinity-chest science rig apart, or which of them mattered.", "3) Only the red science fix finished (a reversed belt at 46.5,2.5). The coal automation isn't built: the only coal is about 210 belt tiles from the boilers at [gps=-27,-43], and I'd just gathered 400 plates and queued 4 drills when you stopped me. 4) Next time I'd check production and the power/lab chain first, and ask which stopgaps count before scoping a 200-tile belt."], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
