{"run": "20261020-023940-t-deliver-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-deliver", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.197, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 30, "obj_secs": {"chest-filled": 301}, "think_min": 1.0, "idle_min": 2.5, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 13, "extra_looks": 6, "waste": 0.233, "cost_per_met": 0.197, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:take", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 2.55, "hand building": 0.48, "waiting on jobs": 0.09, "crafting/fetching": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 1.03}, "by_tool": {"say": 7, "find": 5, "inspect": 4, "act": 4, "wait": 4, "look": 3, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "map": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to hand-crafting (about 4 min of queued belts, gears, circuits) and the two long walks for plates, to the iron furnaces near (74,30) and the copper furnaces near (14,91).", "2) Missing: a list of where plates were stocked. I found them by scanning furnaces, and copper only turned up after I'd walked to the ore patch.", "3) Confusing: the craft queue made 50 extra belts (100 instead of 50) and the inserter craft stopped at 4, so I crafted 16 more. I never opened the chest to check what was in it before or after.", "4) Next time: check the craft queue before adding to it, and read a chest before and after delivering. I'd also mark plate stock locations so the next run starts with them."], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-023917-t-brownout-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-brownout", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.665, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 73, "obj_secs": {"power-steady": 241}, "think_min": 2.3, "idle_min": 1.1, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 3, "looks": 41, "extra_looks": 27, "waste": 0.411, "cost_per_met": 0.665, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:rotate", "act:take", "build", "designs", "diagnose", "find", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "notes", "production", "recipes", "say", "stop", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 1.35, "idle (nothing running)": 1.14, "blueprint/line building": 0.4, "crafting/fetching": 0.1, "walking": 0.08, "looking": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 2.33}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 14, "act": 13, "say": 8, "map": 8, "find": 7, "look": 5, "diagnose": 4, "wait": 4, "production": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "recipes": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to tracing belts by hand (map plus inspect, tile by tile) to find the dead-end at the copper ore belt and the mis-turned iron belt. 2) Missing: a belt-trace tool that follows a belt from A and reports where it ends or blocks, and a hint of which chests are stock.", "3) Confusing: coordinates from alerts and the map header (tile vs centre, row = y) needed care; diagnose \"no_fuel\" on furnaces hid that the real block was belt geometry. 4) Unfinished: I never confirmed iron plates reach the base, and the north boiler is still hand-fed. 5) Next time: check production and diagnose first, then trace the belts end to end before building anything."], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-024251-d4-library-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "d4-library", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.076, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 11, "obj_secs": {"two-more-smelters": 121}, "think_min": 0.2, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 3, "extra_looks": 0, "waste": 0.0, "cost_per_met": 0.076, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "build", "find_space", "look", "say", "zone"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.94, "hand building": 0.16, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.18}, "by_tool": {"say": 3, "look": 2, "zone": 2, "build": 2, "find_space": 1, "act": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to the two stamps, about 30s each, and the second one said \"paused\" even though it had built all 48 pieces. 2) Nothing was missing for the stamp job, but I had to guess the 24-wide footprint and check it with find_space. I also had no tool to see which pole connects a build to the grid, so I inferred power from the inserter status. 3) The alerts were noisy. They flagged 36 unfueled furnaces and an empty boiler that I couldn't fix by belt in that run. 4) I never put a task on the board or sent a progress update, because both jobs were short. 5) Next time I'd check the boiler fuel and coal supply first, since the build was pointless without power, and I'd post a done_when task for the smelter job."], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-024006-t-deliver-sonnet-i2", "scenario": "t-deliver", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.192, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 36, "obj_secs": {"chest-filled": 301}, "think_min": 1.0, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 12, "extra_looks": 6, "waste": 0.194, "cost_per_met": 0.192, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 3.42, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "hand building": 0.24, "walking": 0.19, "crafting/fetching": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 1.01}, "by_tool": {"say": 9, "act": 8, "wait": 5, "look": 4, "find": 4, "inspect": 4, "techs": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: the order took longest because the base had no copper plates. I walked about 90 tiles each way and hand-mined and smelted 30 plates for the inserters' circuits.", "I was missing a view of stock (no marks, no list of what chests hold) and any copper smelting. I started with almost nothing in my inventory.", "Confusing: the \"look\" at a position returned data around me rather than that spot. Also, I couldn't tell what \"them\" meant in your \"take them from stock or craft them\" message.", "Next time I'd list every chest first and ask what the stock holds before walking out. I'd also queue the belt crafting at the start and mine the copper in parallel. I never fixed the real problem: the boilers and furnaces are hand-fed coal with no coal belt, and research is idle."], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-023815-t-brownout-sonnet-i1", "scenario": "t-brownout", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.368, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 53, "obj_secs": {"power-steady": 301}, "think_min": 2.4, "idle_min": 0.5, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 3, "looks": 25, "extra_looks": 11, "waste": 0.283, "cost_per_met": 0.368, "top_failures": [["FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory", 2], ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", "FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.89, "idle (nothing running)": 0.52, "crafting/fetching": 0.34, "waiting on jobs": 0.23, "walking": 0.12, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 2.38}, "by_tool": {"act": 13, "inspect": 13, "wait": 7, "look": 6, "say": 6, "find": 3, "diagnose": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "map": 1}, "debrief": [], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-024426-d4-library-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "d4-library", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.102, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 1.0, "calls": 17, "obj_secs": {"two-more-smelters": 60}, "think_min": 0.4, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 5, "extra_looks": 1, "waste": 0.059, "cost_per_met": 0.102, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:research", "act:take", "build", "find", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "say", "stamp", "techs", "zone"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.68, "hand building": 0.15, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.37}, "by_tool": {"say": 4, "look": 2, "zone": 2, "stamp": 2, "act": 2, "find_space": 1, "build": 1, "inspect": 1, "find": 1, "techs": 1}, "debrief": ["Fixed the dead boiler at [gps=-31.5,-43] by hand-fueling it, and queued research-speed-1. Research can't actually progress yet. No science packs are being made, and the boiler coal chest is hand-filled, so it will run dry. Coal is also out at the new smelters. Proposed next: automate coal from the nearest patch to the boilers, or build red science. Which first?", "Debrief: 1) The smelter stamps took the most time, about 40s of building; the rest was mostly reading state. 2) I was missing a quick base overview. The look output was huge and the alerts didn't say where the coal or the science supply was. 3) I queued research-speed-1 blind, and the labs were starved of both automation and logistic packs, so it was a wasted pick. I should have checked which packs could be made first. 4) The boiler coal chest is hand-filled, so my fix was only a stopgap and will run dry. 5) Next time I'd start with production, diagnose and the coal supply before touching anything, and build the coal belt before fueling by hand."], "phase": "train-8", "cycle": 8}
{"run": "20261020-024604-t-power-line-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-power-line", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.28, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 35, "obj_secs": {"power-the-block": 121}, "think_min": 1.1, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 15, "extra_looks": 7, "waste": 0.2, "cost_per_met": 0.28, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:take", "build", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "lesson", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.48, "blueprint/line building": 0.45, "walking": 0.32, "waiting on jobs": 0.1, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.13}, "by_tool": {"say": 9, "act": 6, "look": 5, "find": 4, "inspect": 3, "map": 2, "techs": 1, "build": 1, "diagnose": 1, "marks": 1, "wait": 1, "lesson": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/4: The pole line to the gear assemblers was quick (one build line call). Most of my time went on walking 150+ tiles each way and hand-fueling about 40 burner drills and furnaces one insert at a time.", "2/4: I was missing a tool that lists every entity that's out of fuel with its position, and a way to fuel a whole area in one action. One inspect call at the coal field returned a huge dump of ore tiles that buried the useful entities.", "3/4: I fueled the furnaces from positions I read off the ASCII map and never verified them afterward. Some may have been missed, and the drill at [gps=35,101] is still empty. I also let long gaps pass without a chat update.", "4/4: Next time I'd verify after fueling, and put the coal feed (an inserter and a belt into the boilers) on the board as a real task before hand-fueling. The labs have no science packs, and I never got to fix that."], "phase": "train-9", "cycle": 9}
{"run": "20261020-024604-t-power-line-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-power-line", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.35, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 44, "obj_secs": {"power-the-block": 121}, "think_min": 1.8, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 22, "extra_looks": 12, "waste": 0.273, "cost_per_met": 0.35, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:take", "board", "build", "designs", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "production", "say", "stamp", "techs", "wait", "work", "zone"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.78, "waiting on jobs": 0.48, "walking": 0.43, "hand building": 0.15, "looking": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.84}, "by_tool": {"say": 6, "find": 6, "look": 5, "act": 5, "inspect": 4, "map": 4, "wait": 2, "build": 2, "diagnose": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "work": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: the power line to [gps=128,-51] worked quickly (10 small poles). Most of my time went to finding where things were, because the copper chain was half-built. Copper ore runs by belt to [gps=0,79] and had no smelter. I stamped and built a 12-furnace smelting column at [gps=0,72]. It isn't tested, and I haven't hooked up coal or the plate output belt.", "Missing: a map or overview of the existing belt lines, and a note on which item is on which lane. Confusing: look centers on me rather than a point, and the alerts pointed at burner drills that are legacy stopgaps. Next time I'd check production and diagnose before walking anywhere. Still open: the coal belt at [gps=23,103] has to be joined to the ore belt, and the boilers are hand-fed."], "phase": "train-9", "cycle": 9}
{"run": "20261020-024604-t-belt-ore-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-belt-ore", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.197, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 33, "obj_secs": {"ore-to-furnaces": 241}, "think_min": 0.9, "idle_min": 0.7, "failed_calls": 4, "undone": 0, "looks": 12, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.212, "cost_per_met": 0.197, "top_failures": [["FAILED nothing to take from transport-belt (iron-ore) (it holds nothing); no chest or mach", 5], ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 2]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED nothing to take from transport-belt (iron-ore) (it holds nothing); no chest or mach", "exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "stop", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.67, "waiting on jobs": 0.64, "failed calls": 0.31, "blueprint/line building": 0.3, "hand building": 0.02, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.89}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 9, "say": 7, "act": 4, "wait": 4, "build": 3, "map": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "stop": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on getting 2 underground belts. I started with almost nothing, and the plates I needed to craft them were not lying around.", "2) Missing: a stock of plates or belts at the start, and a way to see which chests held spare materials. The belts that showed up in my inventory were a surprise, and I didn't know where they came from.", "3) Confusing: the build line tool placed belts one tile off from the drill belt end (y -43.5 vs -42.5) and one tile short at the furnace input. I only caught both by inspecting the belts afterward. The take op on ore-loaded belts also reported they held nothing.", "4) Next time: inspect the exact last-belt coordinates of both ends before calling line, and check the inventory for undergrounds first. I'd also fix the boiler fuel and burner coal supply earlier, since that stalls the base more than the ore belt did."], "phase": "train-9", "cycle": 9}
{"run": "20261020-024604-t-belt-ore-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-belt-ore", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.253, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 40, "obj_secs": {"ore-to-furnaces": 302}, "think_min": 0.9, "idle_min": 1.7, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 17, "extra_looks": 7, "waste": 0.2, "cost_per_met": 0.253, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait", "work"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 1.67, "walking": 0.65, "hand building": 0.58, "failed calls": 0.22, "blueprint/line building": 0.05, "crafting/fetching": 0.02, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.95}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 9, "act": 7, "say": 6, "wait": 5, "map": 4, "look": 2, "find": 2, "build": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "work": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to walking ~90 tiles to base chests for belts and undergrounds, since I carried nothing. 2) Missing: a stocked supply chest near the build site, and a way to see where an existing belt actually ends.", "3) Confusing: the line tool's endpoints were off by one row from the real belts, which left two one-tile gaps; I only found them by mapping the belt after it was built. 4) Next time I'd check the line tool's start and end tiles against the map first, carry spare belts and undergrounds, and read the fuel/power alerts before starting."], "phase": "train-9", "cycle": 9}
{"run": "20261020-024912-t-cross-bus-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-cross-bus", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.172, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 25, "obj_secs": {"copper-across-bus": 181}, "think_min": 0.7, "idle_min": 0.4, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 12, "extra_looks": 5, "waste": 0.24, "cost_per_met": 0.172, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:take", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.4, "blueprint/line building": 0.32, "failed calls": 0.08, "hand building": 0.01, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.68}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 7, "say": 6, "look": 2, "build": 2, "find": 2, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "act": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: the most time went to finding materials. I started with 8 plates and had to look for the stock chests, which turned out to be at about [gps=-10,-28]. I was missing underground belts until I found them there. The build line tool did the actual routing and bus crossing in one call. Confusing: the first look showed me at 0,0 and then I was suddenly at the stock chests, and the status alerts kept repeating. Next time I'd check marked or stock chests first and read the chest's inserter orientation before touching the belt end. I'd also say sooner that the belt was already done."], "phase": "train-9", "cycle": 9}
{"run": "20261020-025019-t-smelter-column-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-smelter-column", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.248, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 31, "obj_secs": {"eight-furnaces": 241}, "think_min": 1.8, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 12, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.161, "cost_per_met": 0.248, "top_failures": [["FAILED nothing to take from iron-chest (pipe) (it holds N pipe); nearest with pipe: N at N", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED nothing to take from iron-chest (pipe) (it holds N pipe); nearest with pipe: N at N"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "designs", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "skill_read", "stop", "techs", "wait", "work"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.63, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "failed calls": 0.08, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "own scripts": 0.0, "thinking": 1.75}, "by_tool": {"say": 7, "inspect": 5, "act": 5, "look": 3, "find": 2, "work": 1, "map": 1, "designs": 1, "skill_read": 1, "marks": 1, "stop": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/3: Most time went to finding materials. I started with nearly nothing and had to scout for the depot chests near [gps=-10,-27] before I could build anything.", "Debrief 2/3: I was missing a stock list up front (marks was empty) and info on whether the ore belt actually had ore and coal. Confusing: stone furnaces showed \"fuel none\" at first, and the alerts about power and the idle labs pulled me away from the order.", "Debrief 3/3: Nothing failed outright, but one early act was queued as a long batch and I had to stop it to fix the boiler. Next time I'd check the depot and power first, and mark the stock chests. Open items: boiler coal is hand-fed, the x=74 furnaces have no fuel, and nothing is researching."], "phase": "train-9", "cycle": 9}
{"run": "20261020-025005-t-cross-bus-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-cross-bus", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.152, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 25, "obj_secs": {"copper-across-bus": 181}, "think_min": 0.7, "idle_min": 0.4, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 12, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.2, "cost_per_met": 0.152, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:place", "act:take", "board", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.44, "blueprint/line building": 0.32, "hand building": 0.09, "failed calls": 0.08, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.74}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 6, "say": 4, "act": 3, "look": 2, "map": 2, "build": 2, "find": 2, "wait": 2, "board": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": [], "phase": "train-9", "cycle": 9}
{"run": "20261020-025226-t-gear-cell-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-gear-cell", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.214, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 28, "obj_secs": {"gear-cell": 181}, "think_min": 1.3, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 10, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.143, "cost_per_met": 0.214, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "board", "designs", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "recipes", "say", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.46, "crafting/fetching": 0.08, "waiting on jobs": 0.03, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 1.33}, "by_tool": {"say": 8, "inspect": 5, "act": 4, "look": 2, "find": 2, "wait": 2, "board": 1, "marks": 1, "recipes": 1, "designs": 1, "map": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: most time went to walking, about 130 tiles each way between the supply depot at [gps=-12,-28] and the belt site, plus a detour to refuel the boiler.", "Missing: I started with almost nothing and had to find the depot by scanning around. Knowing which chests were shared stock up front would have saved that. A way to ask for parts, like a requester chest at the site, would have helped too.", "Confusing: the queued act chain returned \"still running\" while I was mid-walk, and the first look showed no entities near the target. The map and inspect worked fine once I was there. Also, the inserter pickup and drop coordinates the tool reported were slightly off-tile, though they worked.", "Next time: grab all parts and a coal stack in one trip. Write the pole and assembler layout before walking, so the build is a single batch. Fuel the boiler on the way past instead of afterwards. And I'd flag the hand-fed boiler coal as the real power risk to fix with a coal belt."], "phase": "train-9", "cycle": 9}
