{"run": "20261020-025442-t-gear-cell-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-gear-cell", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.21, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 32, "obj_secs": {"gear-cell": 241}, "think_min": 1.4, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 0, "looks": 13, "extra_looks": 6, "waste": 0.25, "cost_per_met": 0.21, "top_failures": [["FAILED cancelled: replaced", 1], ["FAILED create_entity failed for splitter", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cancelled: replaced", "FAILED create_entity failed for splitter"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "recipes", "say", "wait", "work"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 0.41, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "crafting/fetching": 0.1, "hand building": 0.03, "failed calls": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.39}, "by_tool": {"say": 6, "inspect": 5, "act": 5, "find": 4, "wait": 4, "look": 2, "map": 2, "marks": 2, "work": 1, "recipes": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to walking: I had nothing in my inventory, so I made a 100-tile round trip to the stock chests at [gps=-12,-28] for an assembler, inserters, poles and a splitter. 2) I was missing a way to know where spare parts live; I found the depot only by inspecting chests one radius at a time.", "3) What confused me: a move I replaced kept running to its old target, so I ended up at odd positions. The first splitter placement also failed with no reason given, and I had to mine the belt tile under it. 4) Next time I'd check the depot first, take everything for the job in one trip, and set a chest limit on the gear chest. I never measured the gear rate."], "phase": "train-9", "cycle": 9}
{"run": "20261020-025803-t-inserter-mall-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-inserter-mall", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.12, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 16, "obj_secs": {"inserter-mall": 121}, "think_min": 0.6, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 5, "extra_looks": 0, "waste": 0.062, "cost_per_met": 0.12, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "act:wait", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"failed calls": 0.27, "waiting on jobs": 0.2, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.6}, "by_tool": {"say": 6, "inspect": 3, "act": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to working out the layout without new poles, so I placed the assembler and inserters inside the two existing poles' reach.", "2) I was missing wood and copper for poles, and I started with almost nothing. Taking plates, gears and circuits from the infinity chests solved the parts, but I only guessed that was allowed.", "3) Nothing failed except the pole craft. The place result printed inserter drops like -53.5,86.7, which confused me for a moment; it did land in the assembler.", "4) Next time I'd check what the nearby chests hold and which poles reach before crafting anything. I'd also have asked sooner about the boiler, fuel and idle-lab alerts, which I never touched."], "phase": "train-9", "cycle": 9}
{"run": "20261020-025543-t-red-block-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-red-block", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.357, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 39, "obj_secs": {"red-block": 301}, "think_min": 1.7, "idle_min": 1.6, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 14, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.103, "cost_per_met": 0.357, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "designs", "diagnose", "find", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait", "work"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 1.58, "hand building": 0.44, "walking": 0.23, "waiting on jobs": 0.06, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "crafting/fetching": 0.0, "thinking": 1.71}, "by_tool": {"say": 9, "act": 8, "look": 6, "wait": 4, "inspect": 3, "diagnose": 2, "techs": 1, "designs": 1, "marks": 1, "find_space": 1, "work": 1, "map": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on figuring out the state I woke into (fresh session, no roadmap) and finding that labs were 120 tiles from the science assembler. 2) Missing: a map-wide overview of what exists and where the labs are, plus enough iron (only 96) for a 125-belt run. 3) Confusing: the gear assembler had an inserter dropping onto bare ground at the west side, which I left alone. 4) Failed: nothing broke, but packs still reach labs only by hand, so the science loop isn't truly automated. 5) Next time: build the assemblers next to the labs, or plan the pack belt right away, and stock plates first."], "phase": "train-9", "cycle": 9}
{"run": "20261020-025902-t-inserter-mall-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-inserter-mall", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.116, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 12, "obj_secs": {"inserter-mall": 121}, "think_min": 0.5, "idle_min": 0.2, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 5, "extra_looks": 1, "waste": 0.167, "cost_per_met": 0.116, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:move", "act:place", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"failed calls": 0.27, "idle (nothing running)": 0.22, "hand building": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.55}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 3, "say": 2, "act": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": [], "phase": "train-9", "cycle": 9}
{"run": "20261020-025548-t-red-block-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-red-block", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.429, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 6.0, "calls": 40, "obj_secs": {"red-block": 362}, "think_min": 2.9, "idle_min": 2.9, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 12, "extra_looks": 2, "waste": 0.05, "cost_per_met": 0.429, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:configure", "act:craft", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "designs", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "production", "say", "techs", "wait", "work"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 2.87, "hand building": 0.46, "waiting on jobs": 0.2, "crafting/fetching": 0.03, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 2.93}, "by_tool": {"say": 9, "act": 8, "wait": 7, "inspect": 4, "look": 3, "map": 2, "find": 2, "work": 1, "designs": 1, "marks": 1, "production": 1, "techs": 1}, "debrief": ["Two labs now at [gps=-8,90] right next to the red pack chest, both working; queued radar, physical damage 1, heavy armor (red-only techs). 24 packs/min feeds ~2 labs. Green science is the next unlock for most techs; want me on that, or the boiler/fuel outages first?", "Debrief 1/3: Most time went to hand-crafting 6 assemblers, 14 inserters and poles, plus walking about 100 tiles from spawn to the belts. Most of that was waiting on the craft queue.", "Debrief 2/3: Missing a designs-library entry that matched \"red science off two belts\". The built-in red-science-5 assumes gears already on a belt, so I hand-placed the layout. I also had no assembler stock to take, and inspect on a belt area dumps huge output.", "Debrief 3/3: What confused me: a pole's supply area didn't cover inserters I put on the far side. Also, I told you 0.4 packs/s when four assemblers at 0.1/s each make 0.4/s only if the number is per second; production showed 24/min, which is 0.1/s per assembler times 4 = 0.4/s... so my \"design\" claim was fine, but I'd measure first. Next time: copy this block into the library, build the labs in the same pass, and use build kind=stamp instead of placing by hand.", "Correction to 3/3: 24 packs/min is 0.4/s, which is exactly the design rate. My earlier \"ceiling\" remark was muddled."], "phase": "train-9", "cycle": 9}
{"run": "20261020-030027-t-steel-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-steel", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.24, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 6.0, "calls": 33, "obj_secs": {"steel": 362}, "think_min": 1.3, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 0, "looks": 10, "extra_looks": 5, "waste": 0.212, "cost_per_met": 0.24, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1], ["FAILED steel-axe isn't researched in labs; it unlocks when you craft-item steel-plate xN (", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", "FAILED steel-axe isn't researched in labs; it unlocks when you craft-item steel-plate xN ("], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:take", "act:wait", "board", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 1.43, "hand building": 1.01, "crafting/fetching": 0.55, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "failed calls": 0.02, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.3}, "by_tool": {"say": 9, "act": 7, "find": 4, "wait": 4, "inspect": 3, "look": 1, "board": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "diagnose": 1, "techs": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: most time went to walking about 100 tiles each way and gathering raw materials by hand. I started with almost nothing: mined stone and copper ore, smelted copper for inserter circuits, and crafted every inserter and chest myself.", "Missing: a stocked chest with inserters, furnaces, poles and wood. The infinity chests at the belt held only iron and coal, so I had no copper source near the build site, and I was short on wood for poles.", "Confusing: I couldn't queue the steel-axe research because it unlocks by crafting 50 steel plates by hand. Also, the 4/min steel figure was a 10-minute average, so I misread it until it settled at 16/min.", "Next time: check what the base can supply first, carry a build kit to the site, and fuel the dead boiler before anything else. The boiler is a stopgap, since I only hand-fed 20 coal and it needs a coal belt. Nothing makes science packs yet, so the labs stay starved."], "phase": "train-9", "cycle": 9}
{"run": "20261020-030339-t-starved-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-starved", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.274, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 34, "obj_secs": {"red-running": 120}, "think_min": 1.5, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 1, "looks": 15, "extra_looks": 9, "waste": 0.294, "cost_per_met": 0.274, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 0.73, "idle (nothing running)": 0.25, "hand building": 0.19, "walking": 0.09, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.49}, "by_tool": {"act": 9, "say": 8, "inspect": 7, "look": 4, "diagnose": 2, "techs": 1, "wait": 1, "find": 1, "map": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/3: The copper belt fix was quick. Most time went on tracing why the labs starved. The red science at [gps=51,5] has no output path and the labs sit about 70 tiles away. I moved the labs to [gps=60,8] and added pack output inserters on 2 of the 3 assemblers, but I haven't verified packs reaching the labs.", "Debrief 2/3: I was missing iron plates (I had 8, so I could only craft 4 inserters), which is why the third assembler at [gps=55,5] has no output inserter. I also had no clear picture of the base layout. The infinity chests, the fake power source and the 33 chests made it hard to tell what was real supply. The look and inspect radius is small, and the belt-trace script is slow over long distances.", "Debrief 3/3: Next time I'd map the whole chain from ore to lab first, then check what ops considers real supply. Still open: the 32 out-of-fuel burner drills near [gps=74,69] need electric drills or a coal belt, and the idle lab-side gear assemblers at [gps=-20,-33] have no iron."], "phase": "train-9", "cycle": 9}
