{"run": "20261020-030925-t-deliver-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-deliver", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.276, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 31, "obj_secs": {"chest-filled": 181}, "think_min": 0.9, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 0, "looks": 16, "extra_looks": 10, "waste": 0.387, "cost_per_met": 0.276, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1], ["error: no entity called electronic-circuit", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", "error: no entity called electronic-circuit"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:take", "act:wait", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "production", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 1.34, "hand building": 0.23, "crafting/fetching": 0.17, "walking": 0.08, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 0.92}, "by_tool": {"find": 6, "say": 6, "act": 6, "inspect": 5, "look": 3, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "production": 1, "map": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to walking, hand-feeding fuel and hand-crafting, so there wasn't enough automation. 2) I was missing a steady coal/plate supply and a clear roadmap or board; research sat idle (labs 0/2, no science made). 3) Confusing: burner smelter arrays need manual coal, and ghost and roboport behaviour is easy to get wrong. 4) Next time I'd set up electric drills plus a coal belt first, then automate red science early, and use stamps instead of hand-placing."], "phase": "train-9", "cycle": 9}
{"run": "20261020-030716-t-brownout-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-brownout", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.539, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 62, "obj_secs": {"power-steady": 241}, "think_min": 2.9, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 3, "undone": 1, "looks": 29, "extra_looks": 12, "waste": 0.258, "cost_per_met": 0.539, "top_failures": [["FAILED cannot craft steam-engine: missing ingredients", 1], ["FAILED no steam-engine in inventory", 1], ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", 1], ["FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory", 1], ["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft small-electric-pole: missing ingredients", "FAILED cannot craft steam-engine: missing ingredients", "FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory", "FAILED no steam-engine in inventory", "error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:rotate", "act:take", "build", "designs", "diagnose", "find", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "skill_run", "stamp", "stop", "techs", "wait", "zone"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 1.37, "walking": 0.72, "hand building": 0.4, "waiting on jobs": 0.09, "failed calls": 0.01, "looking": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "own scripts": 0.0, "thinking": 2.88}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 14, "act": 12, "say": 10, "find": 6, "look": 5, "map": 2, "stamp": 2, "build": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "diagnose": 1, "skill_run": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/4: Most time went to tracing why nothing worked: the copper ore belt at [gps=0,79] just ended with no smelter, and coal sat unused on a parallel belt. Building was quick once I knew that (stamped a smelting column, merged coal, ran a 115-tile belt).", "2/4: Missing info: a map of what each far-flung build was meant to do and where the copper plates should go. I also had no copper to craft poles, and the science area's layout is hand-fed and awkward to hook a belt into.", "3/4: Confusing/failed: the ASCII map coordinates are easy to misread by one tile, so my belt end at [gps=-17,-31] dead-ends into an assembler (belts can't insert). I was mid-fix, rerouting it to an inserter at the red science assembler [gps=-20,-33]. Copper plates are now made (225/min) but not yet delivered, so labs are still idle. Note the boiler at [gps=-31,-43] is only hand-fed.", "4/4: Next time: inspect each belt's far end first, verify exact tile positions with inspect before planning around the map, and stamp a proper red-science block on the copper line instead of retrofitting the old hand-fed one. The iron burner array at [gps=74,69] also needs electric drills plus a coal belt."], "phase": "train-9", "cycle": 9}
