{"run": "20261020-034325-t-smelter-column-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-smelter-column", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.288, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 3.0, "calls": 32, "obj_secs": {"eight-furnaces": 181}, "think_min": 1.1, "idle_min": 0.7, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 14, "extra_looks": 7, "waste": 0.219, "cost_per_met": 0.288, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "build", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.74, "hand building": 0.1, "blueprint/line building": 0.04, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 1.1}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 9, "say": 8, "act": 3, "wait": 3, "look": 2, "build": 2, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "diagnose": 1, "find": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to the long walk to the stock chests and placing 16 inserters and 8 poles one at a time; one stamp of a furnace-column design would have been faster.", "2) I was missing a view of the shared stock up front (I had to walk there and inspect each chest) and any info on whether the ore belt carried enough coal; at first the coal lane was empty and only 2 furnaces had fuel.", "3) Confusing: inserter place results report the drop as y+0.7, and I wasn't sure the belt-turn connect at the corner would work. It did. Inspect on a radius of 10 also returns huge output.", "4) Next time: check the coal supply on the belt before building, copy the finished column into my design library (I didn't), and hold my first report until the coal had been checked for a few minutes."], "phase": "train-10", "cycle": 10}
