{"run": "20261020-041716-t-starved-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-starved", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.292, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 35, "obj_secs": {"red-running": 120}, "think_min": 1.7, "idle_min": 1.4, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 1, "looks": 14, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.171, "cost_per_met": 0.292, "top_failures": [["FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "designs", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "production", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 1.4, "hand building": 0.17, "walking": 0.15, "waiting on jobs": 0.08, "crafting/fetching": 0.01, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 1.67}, "by_tool": {"act": 8, "look": 6, "inspect": 6, "say": 5, "wait": 5, "techs": 1, "find": 1, "designs": 1, "marks": 1, "production": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: (1) Hand-crafting the labs took the most time, mostly copper cable and circuits, plus the walk to the iron field at [gps=75,66] for plates. (2) I was missing a way to see what the rig was meant to feed. The packs had no output path, and the real labs at [gps=-22,-37] were 80 tiles away on a dying steam boiler. (3) The belt fix was quick, but the result said nothing about the missing output. I only found that by reading the inserters. look also centers on me, so I wasted a call by passing x,y to it. (4) Now: packs go straight from the assemblers into 2 labs by inserter, and both labs are working. I took one assembler out for a lab, so the rig makes fewer packs. (5) Next time I'd check the whole chain from pack to lab before touching anything. I'd also grab plates and craft the labs first, while walking."], "phase": "train-11", "cycle": 11}
{"run": "20261020-041755-t-starved-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-starved", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.39, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 50, "obj_secs": {"red-running": 120}, "think_min": 1.7, "idle_min": 1.0, "failed_calls": 2, "undone": 2, "looks": 24, "extra_looks": 10, "waste": 0.28, "cost_per_met": 0.39, "top_failures": [["FAILED in Ns, N tool calls", 1], ["error: stopped: a human said something", 1], ["FAILED cannot place inserter at N,N: blocked by small-electric-pole@N,N", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot place inserter at N,N: blocked by small-electric-pole@N,N", "FAILED in Ns, N tool calls", "error: stopped: a human said something"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "post_task", "say", "skill_run", "stop", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.96, "walking": 0.32, "waiting on jobs": 0.31, "hand building": 0.1, "own scripts": 0.02, "crafting/fetching": 0.01, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 1.74}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 9, "act": 7, "say": 7, "look": 6, "wait": 5, "find": 5, "skill_run": 4, "map": 2, "diagnose": 2, "techs": 1, "post_task": 1, "stop": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to tracing belts by hand (follow_belt/probe) to find two dead ends: the copper tile at 46,2 and the iron corner at 71,-26. Both fixed by rotating one belt.", "2) Missing: a tool that shows where a belt line stops or breaks, and a plain map of what feeds the lab block. Walking 100+ tiles also ate time. 3) Confusing: labs sit far from the test rig, and the lab block's science gear assembler is fed from an empty chest at [gps=-13,-33] that nothing fills.", "4) Not finished: labs still get no packs. I had belts/inserters ready to tap the iron belt at [gps=-5,-26] and feed that chest. Coal is still hand-fed for boilers and furnaces, and the coal field is ~120 tiles south. Next time I'd trace the whole chain once, then build, not fix piecemeal."], "phase": "train-11", "cycle": 11}
{"run": "20261020-042104-t-deliver-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-deliver", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.162, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 1.0, "calls": 21, "obj_secs": {"chest-filled": 60}, "think_min": 0.4, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 7, "extra_looks": 4, "waste": 0.238, "cost_per_met": 0.162, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:take", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "status", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.16, "waiting on jobs": 0.15, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 0.45}, "by_tool": {"say": 7, "inspect": 4, "act": 3, "look": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1, "find": 1, "status": 1, "wait": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: most time went into finding stock, because my inventory was nearly empty and `look` showed no chest contents. I had to inspect a radius around [gps=-10,-28] to find the belts and inserters.", "Missing: a quick way to list stock chests by item. `marks` was empty, and a \"where is X\" search would have helped. I also tried to call `research` and `look` as tools or act ops, which don't exist; I got a validation error and moved on.", "Open problems I only patched: the boiler at [gps=-31.5,-43] has no inserter and was hand-fed, and 32 furnaces/drills near [gps=74,69] are out of fuel. Labs have no red science, so nothing is researching.", "Next time: after the quick order, I'd go straight to the root cause. That means a coal belt to the boilers and a working red science feed, instead of asking first. I also should have verified the boiler was running after fueling it."], "phase": "train-11", "cycle": 11}
{"run": "20261020-042142-t-deliver-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "t-deliver", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.139, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 1.0, "calls": 22, "obj_secs": {"chest-filled": 60}, "think_min": 0.4, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 11, "extra_looks": 6, "waste": 0.318, "cost_per_met": 0.139, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called iron-plate (did you mean iron-chest, iron-ore, iron-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:take", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "techs"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.4, "walking": 0.14, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 0.4}, "by_tool": {"say": 6, "find": 5, "look": 4, "act": 3, "inspect": 2, "techs": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to finding materials. I started with an empty inventory, and plates and stock were scattered across chests I had to inspect one by one. 2) Missing: a one-call \"what's in all chests\" overview, and any coal near the boilers. `marks` was empty and `find` can't search items inside chests. 3) Confusing: the alerts showed 32 unfueled machines and an idle base, but the real cause is a hand-fed coal design. 4) The inserter/belt order went fine. The boiler fix was only a stopgap with 30 coal. 5) Next time: build the electric-drill coal belt first, then red science. I'd also mark the stock chests so the whole crew can find them."], "phase": "train-11", "cycle": 11}
