{"run": "20261020-042325-d4-library-sonnet-i6", "scenario": "d4-library", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.092, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 13, "obj_secs": {"two-more-smelters": 121}, "think_min": 0.6, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 3, "extra_looks": 0, "waste": 0.0, "cost_per_met": 0.092, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "build", "find_space", "look", "say", "stop", "techs"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 1.2, "other": 0.0, "hand building": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.55}, "by_tool": {"say": 4, "build": 3, "look": 2, "techs": 1, "find_space": 1, "act": 1, "stop": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) The stamps took the most time (about 40s each); the controller fetched and crafted everything itself, which worked well.\n2) I started with almost no items and didn't know where the build materials came from until it ran.\n3) The second stamp reported \"paused\" with 48 built, and I needed a re-call to confirm it was done. That was a little confusing.\n4) The alerts (boiler out of fuel, 32 burners out of coal, no research) were never addressed. I was about to fuel the boiler when you stopped me.\n5) Next time I'd check alerts and power before building, and I'd report the stamp coordinates in one line."], "phase": "train-11", "cycle": 11}
