a pole.", "3/4: What went wrong: the new copper belt from [gps=5,65] to [gps=9.5,-25.5] feeds the trunk from the south side, which is the iron lane, so copper and iron will mix on one lane. Brownout also came back, since the north boiler is still hand-fed and the south plant is at capacity.", "4/4: Next time I'd check power and fuel first, ask where lanes are meant to go before routing a belt, and put the copper join on the north side of the trunk. Open items: the copper smelter at [gps=0,72] is built, the 32 unfueled burner drills at [gps=76,69] still need a coal belt, and the north boiler needs an inserter."], "phase": "train-11", "cycle": 11}
