{"run": "20261020-044213-t-red-block-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-red-block", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.406, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 40, "obj_secs": {"red-block": 301}, "think_min": 2.2, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 14, "extra_looks": 3, "waste": 0.1, "cost_per_met": 0.406, "top_failures": [["FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED no small-electric-pole in inventory"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "act:wait", "designs", "find", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "map", "production", "recipes", "say", "techs", "wait", "work"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 1.13, "hand building": 0.41, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "walking": 0.22, "failed calls": 0.08, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 2.15}, "by_tool": {"say": 9, "act": 8, "look": 5, "inspect": 5, "wait": 3, "techs": 2, "designs": 2, "recipes": 1, "production": 1, "map": 1, "find_space": 1, "work": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on working out what the order meant. \"Red made 28, needs 30\" and \"make gears there too\" gave no location or product, and the red block was already running. 2) Missing: a way to see which pack count the check reads, and where the labs are. They were 123 tiles away and I only found that late. 3) Confusing: the \"red made\" figure looked cumulative while production showed a rate, and I couldn't tell which one the check used. 4) Next time I'll check lab status and pack delivery first, since idle labs were the real bottleneck. I'd also ask for the target in one line before building anything."], "phase": "train-12", "cycle": 12}
