{"run": "20261020-045850-d4-library-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "d4-library", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.092, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 10, "obj_secs": {"two-more-smelters": 121}, "think_min": 0.2, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 3, "extra_looks": 0, "waste": 0.0, "cost_per_met": 0.092, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["build", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "say", "techs", "work"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 1.19, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.23}, "by_tool": {"say": 3, "build": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "find_space": 1, "inspect": 1, "work": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) The stamp took about 40s each; the second one paused once and I had to call build again. 2) I started with almost no inventory (1 drill, 1 furnace, 8 plates), but the stamp fetched or crafted what it needed. 3) I had no way to see a design's footprint or its fuel setup beforehand, so I only found the east furnaces had no coal by inspecting afterwards. 4) The inspect output was huge for a radius of 8, and the alerts (boiler, 32 unfueled furnaces, idle labs) were more urgent than the order. 5) Next time I'd check the stamp's footprint and fuel first, then fix the boiler and queue research right after."], "phase": "train-12", "cycle": 12}
