{"run": "20261020-042720-d2-science-steps-sonnet-i1", "scenario": "d2-science-steps", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": false, "score": 0.8438, "objectives": 4, "met": 3, "cost": 2.933, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 39.1, "calls": 199, "obj_secs": {"red-automated": 121, "green-automated": 1201, "six-labs": 422}, "think_min": 15.1, "idle_min": 2.8, "failed_calls": 9, "undone": 5, "looks": 79, "extra_looks": 38, "waste": 0.261, "cost_per_met": 0.978, "top_failures": [["FAILED nothing to take from stone-furnace (iron-plate) (it holds N coal, N iron-ore); near", 6], ["FAILED nothing to take from transport-belt (copper-plate) (it holds nothing); nearest with", 2], ["FAILED nothing to take from iron-chest (coal) (it holds nothing); nearest with coal: N at ", 1], ["FAILED no path to N,N (blocked by water/cliffs/buildings?)", 1], ["FAILED cannot craft assembling-machineN: missing ingredients", 1], ["FAILED cannot craft wooden-chest: missing ingredients", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["FAILED cannot craft assembling-machineN: missing ingredients", "FAILED cannot craft wooden-chest: missing ingredients", "FAILED cannot place assembling-machineN at N,N: blocked by small-electric-pole@N,N", "FAILED no path to N,N (blocked by water/cliffs/buildings?)", "FAILED nothing to take from iron-chest (coal) (it holds nothing); nearest with coal: N at ", "FAILED nothing to take from stone-furnace (iron-plate) (it holds N coal, N iron-ore); near", "FAILED nothing to take from transport-belt (copper-plate) (it holds nothing); nearest with", "FAILED small-electric-pole has no recipe to set", "exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:set_recipe", "act:take", "act:wait", "build", "designs", "diagnose", "find", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "notes", "post_task", "production", "recipes", "say", "skill_run", "stamp", "stop", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"waiting on jobs": 4.85, "idle (nothing running)": 2.84, "crafting/fetching": 2.73, "hand building": 2.61, "walking": 1.96, "blueprint/line building": 1.94, "failed calls": 1.07, "looking": 0.02, "own scripts": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 15.14}, "by_tool": {"act": 58, "inspect": 31, "say": 19, "wait": 15, "look": 13, "find": 11, "build": 11, "map": 10, "diagnose": 8, "production": 5, "notes": 4, "stop": 3}, "debrief": ["6/6 labs working, red and green both made at 12 per minute. I'm idle. Pick one: automate the gear chest feed, build steel, or convert the burner arrays at [gps=80,70] to electric.", "Debrief 1/3: The most time went on getting red science to the labs. Red was the real limit, not the lab count. I spent several rounds on inserter and chain layout, and on hand-feeding the gear chest.", "Debrief 2/3: What I was missing was a quick view of which science techs need which packs. The green used 0 alert was only a red-only queue. Also, inspect output for belts is very verbose, so a summary mode would help.", "Debrief 3/3: My mistakes were putting the long inserter on an inserter tile, and mining a pole that powered other things. Next time I'd check pickup and drop tiles and power wiring before placing, and automate the iron feed instead of hand-filling it. Two stopgaps are still open: the hand-filled gear chest and the hand-fueled burner arrays."], "phase": "train-12", "cycle": 12}
{"run": "20261020-050649-t-power-line-sonnet-i4", "scenario": "t-power-line", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.168, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 22, "obj_secs": {"power-the-block": 121}, "think_min": 0.4, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 11, "extra_looks": 5, "waste": 0.227, "cost_per_met": 0.168, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:take", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "post_task", "say", "techs", "update_task"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 0.45, "walking": 0.37, "hand building": 0.01, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 0.38}, "by_tool": {"look": 5, "say": 5, "find": 5, "act": 2, "techs": 1, "post_task": 1, "build": 1, "inspect": 1, "update_task": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went on walking, about 150 tiles each way to the boiler. The pole line itself was one build call. 2) I was missing a way to check power on a machine and a quick fuel/coal overview. look doesn't center on a remote x,y, so I had to walk over to see things. 3) The task check \"working\" needed a zone, so it never closed. I should have set the zone when I posted it. 4) The alerts (boiler, 32 unfueled burners, iron falling to 19/min) point to a coal supply problem I only patched by hand. 5) Next time I'd post the task with a valid check, then build the coal line first, since power, smelting and research all depend on it."], "phase": "train-13", "cycle": 13}
{"run": "20261020-050649-t-power-line-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-power-line", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.156, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 18, "obj_secs": {"power-the-block": 121}, "think_min": 0.6, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 7, "extra_looks": 2, "waste": 0.111, "cost_per_met": 0.156, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:connect", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:take", "find", "inspect", "look", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.69, "waiting on jobs": 0.11, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.59}, "by_tool": {"look": 5, "say": 5, "act": 3, "techs": 1, "wait": 1, "find": 1, "inspect": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to the pole run to [gps=128,-51] (a long walk) and to waiting on answers about what to do next. 2) I started with almost nothing in my inventory, so I had to fetch poles from the supply chest first. The map had no way to see the grid or which networks were unpowered. 3) The gear assemblers hold plates, but I never confirmed gears came out. The infinity chests and inserters left me unsure what they were doing. 4) The repeated \"no power, no fuel\" alerts pointed to a coal supply problem I could only patch by hand with about 40 coal. 5) Next time I'd check the power and coal alerts first, then connect poles, then build the coal mine and belt before anything else."], "phase": "train-13", "cycle": 13}
{"run": "20261020-050649-t-cross-bus-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-cross-bus", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.193, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 27, "obj_secs": {"copper-across-bus": 241}, "think_min": 1.3, "idle_min": 0.7, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 14, "extra_looks": 7, "waste": 0.296, "cost_per_met": 0.193, "top_failures": [["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and ", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["exception: line failed after N leg(s): route needs N underground-belt but you have N (and "], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:place", "act:take", "build", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.67, "blueprint/line building": 0.32, "failed calls": 0.08, "hand building": 0.08, "crafting/fetching": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "waiting on jobs": 0.0, "thinking": 1.26}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 11, "say": 4, "wait": 3, "build": 2, "act": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "find": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to the copper belt: the first build failed for lack of underground belts, so I fetched belts and iron from the stock chests at [gps=-13,-30]. 2) The line tool started one tile off the real belt end (y=81 vs y=82), so the first run delivered nothing until I added a joining belt. I should have inspected the source belt's exact tile and the delivery lanes right after building. 3) I was missing a clear item inventory (no way to see what's in shared chests without inspecting each one) and a coal supply for the dead boiler at [gps=-31,-43]. 4) Next time I'd check belt coordinates before connecting and verify items arrive before reporting. Open: the boiler is out of fuel, 32 burner machines are out of coal, and no research is running."], "phase": "train-13", "cycle": 13}
