{"run": "20261020-054634-t-starved-sonnet-i5", "scenario": "t-starved", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.332, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 44, "obj_secs": {"red-running": 120}, "think_min": 2.3, "idle_min": 0.6, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 1, "looks": 29, "extra_looks": 21, "waste": 0.5, "cost_per_met": 0.332, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "production", "say", "techs", "wait", "work"], "lost_min": {"idle (nothing running)": 0.59, "walking": 0.25, "hand building": 0.24, "crafting/fetching": 0.11, "looking": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 2.32}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 11, "find": 9, "act": 6, "say": 4, "look": 3, "map": 3, "diagnose": 2, "wait": 2, "techs": 1, "production": 1, "work": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: (1) Most time went to tracing: red science was only a flipped belt at [gps=46,2], but then I found the assemblers at [gps=51,5] have no output inserters, so packs never reach any lab, and the labs sit 80 tiles away at [gps=-25,-37].\n(2) Missing: a map of how the base connects (which belt feeds what), and a cheap way to find stocked chests or furnaces for plates. Inspect and look with big radii also dumped huge ore lists.\n(3) Confusing: the \"red science stopped\" alert was just the first of three problems. The infinity chests supply copper and gears, so I couldn't tell what counts as real supply.\n(4) Not finished: I fueled one boiler by hand, and I was crafting 2 labs and inserters to put labs next to the assemblers.\n(5) Next time: after the first fix, ask what the whole chain is meant to look like, then build the pack-to-lab path before touching anything else."], "phase": "train-14", "cycle": 14}
{"run": "20261020-054614-t-steel-sonnet-i3", "scenario": "t-steel", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.191, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 4.0, "calls": 27, "obj_secs": {"steel": 241}, "think_min": 1.1, "idle_min": 0.3, "failed_calls": 1, "undone": 0, "looks": 9, "extra_looks": 1, "waste": 0.074, "cost_per_met": 0.191, "top_failures": [["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)", 1]], "failure_kinds": ["error: no entity called copper-plate (did you mean copper-ore, copper-stromatolite?)"], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:mine", "act:move", "act:place", "act:take", "act:wait", "board", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "recipes", "say", "status", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 0.86, "waiting on jobs": 0.42, "idle (nothing running)": 0.33, "crafting/fetching": 0.2, "looking": 0.0, "other": 0.0, "failed calls": 0.0, "thinking": 1.12}, "by_tool": {"say": 7, "act": 5, "look": 3, "inspect": 3, "find": 2, "wait": 2, "board": 1, "map": 1, "marks": 1, "recipes": 1, "status": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/3: Most time went on walking and gathering parts. I started with almost nothing, so I had to walk about 60 tiles to hand-mine stone and then take plates and coal from the infinity chests.", "Debrief 2/3: I was missing copper, so I couldn't make circuits or electric inserters. I used burner inserters for output, and they will run out of coal. I also had no stocked chest of building parts and no way to know where stone was without searching.", "Debrief 3/3: Two things confused me. Burner inserters sat idle until they handled coal, so they needed a hand-fed start. Also, a look call showed the belt as 19 tiles one time and 42 the next. Next time I'd check what's on hand first, then mine stone before walking, and tell you up front that the output inserters need swapping once copper exists."], "phase": "train-14", "cycle": 14}
