{"run": "20261020-055131-d4-library-sonnet-i2", "scenario": "d4-library", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.091, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 2.0, "calls": 12, "obj_secs": {"two-more-smelters": 121}, "think_min": 0.4, "idle_min": 0.0, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 0, "looks": 4, "extra_looks": 0, "waste": 0.0, "cost_per_met": 0.091, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["build", "find_space", "inspect", "look", "say", "stamp", "techs", "work"], "lost_min": {"blueprint/line building": 1.19, "other": 0.0, "looking": 0.0, "thinking": 0.36}, "by_tool": {"say": 3, "build": 2, "inspect": 2, "look": 1, "techs": 1, "find_space": 1, "stamp": 1, "work": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief: 1) Most time went to the stamp and build calls, about 40s each, which was fine. 2) I started with almost nothing in my inventory, and the build step fetched and crafted the materials without my help. 3) I confirmed power only by checking that inserters held charge. A direct \"is this on the grid\" check would be clearer. 4) Repeated messages for the same order made me unsure whether anything was new. 5) Next time I'd refuel the boiler and queue research first, since that outage mattered more than the smelters."], "phase": "train-14", "cycle": 14}
{"run": "20261020-054731-t-brownout-sonnet-i1", "scenario": "t-brownout", "commit": "e08d89e", "success": true, "score": 1.0, "objectives": 1, "met": 1, "cost": 0.657, "usage_limit": false, "errors": [], "minutes": 5.0, "calls": 71, "obj_secs": {"power-steady": 301}, "think_min": 2.7, "idle_min": 0.9, "failed_calls": 0, "undone": 1, "looks": 40, "extra_looks": 21, "waste": 0.31, "cost_per_met": 0.657, "top_failures": [], "failure_kinds": [], "ops_used": ["act", "act:craft", "act:insert", "act:move", "act:place", "act:research", "act:rotate", "act:take", "act:wait", "diagnose", "find", "inspect", "look", "map", "marks", "say", "skill_run", "techs", "wait"], "lost_min": {"hand building": 1.14, "idle (nothing running)": 0.91, "crafting/fetching": 0.05, "own scripts": 0.03, "waiting on jobs": 0.01, "looking": 0.01, "other": 0.0, "thinking": 2.71}, "by_tool": {"inspect": 21, "say": 11, "act": 10, "diagnose": 6, "map": 5, "look": 4, "find": 4, "wait": 4, "skill_run": 4, "techs": 1, "marks": 1}, "debrief": ["Debrief 1/3: Most time went on tracing belts by hand (follow_belt, maps, giant inspect dumps). I fixed power at the engine plant with a boiler, 2 engines and a pole. The iron belt had a dead-end corner at [gps=71,-26] and now flows. Science was starved of iron plates, and I never reached copper.", "2/3: Copper is still unfixed. Its ore belt ends at [gps=0,79], short of where I expected the furnaces. I lacked a tool that follows a belt to its end and lists breaks. inspect with radius 12 on an ore field dumped hundreds of ore tiles, and I misjudged tile coordinates twice, once placing a boiler one tile too far.", "3/3: Next time I'd trace the full supply chain with diagnose and one belt walk before touching anything, then fix the root break first. Open items: the copper belt end at [gps=0,79], the north boiler coal chests are hand-filled, and the furnaces at [gps=78,69] are out of coal."], "phase": "train-14", "cycle": 14}
